: an agreement on certain post-signing covenants but that the parties had not reached agreement on the amount of\n667: the Mac-Gray termination fee. The Special Committee also discussed the fact that the exclusivity agreement\n668: would be expiring at 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013 and that CSC/Pamplona had requested an extension of\n669: exclusivity until the end of the day on October 15, 2013. After discussions, the Special Committee determined\n670: that the members of the Transaction Committee and representatives of Goodwin Procter should communicate to the\n671: representative of CSC/Pamplona and representatives at Kirkland, respectively, that the Special Committee\n672: continued to object to the $15 million Mac-Gray termination fee proposed by CSC/Pamplona and would not be\n673: willing to extend exclusivity unless a lower amount were agreed to. The Special Committee confirmed that the\n674: Transaction Committee and representatives of Mac-Gray were authorized to extend the exclusivity agreement\n675: until 11:59 p.m. on ET on October 15, 2013 if CSC/Pamplona would agree to a Mac-Gray termination fee of not\n676: more than $11 million, which represented approximately 3.2% of the total equity value of the transaction.\n677: Later on October 11, 2013, the two members of the Transaction Committee telephoned CSC/Pamplona and\n678: communicated the Special Committee's position. Shortly following that conversation, the representative of\n679: CSC/Pamplona telephoned Mr. Daoust and agreed to the $11 million Mac-Gray\n680: 40\n681: \n682: ========== PAGE 41 (segment 46, zeq=[40]) ==========\n683: Table of Contents\n684: termination fee. Following such agreement, Goodwin Procter delivered Kirkland revised drafts of the merger\n685: agreement and the Pamplona commitment letter.\n686: On October 12, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed a letter agreement extending exclusivity until 11:59\n687: p.m. ET on October 15, 2013.\n688: Between October 12, 2013 and October 14, 2013, Kirkland and Goodwin Procter finalized the remaining unresolved\n689: issues in the merger agreement and the Pamplona commitment letter.\n690: Between October 8, 2013 and October 14, 2013, Kirkland and counsel for Moab negotiated the terms of a voting\n691: agreement for Moab.\n692: On October 14, 2013, the Special Committee held a meeting via teleconference to discuss the final terms of the\n693: transaction and the proposed definitive merger agreement and related documents. By invitation of the Special\n694: Committee, Mr. Rothenberg and representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch and Goodwin Procter were also present for\n695: all or portions of the meeting. The members of the Transaction Committee reported to the Special Committee on\n696: the negotiations that had taken place since the meeting of the Special Committee held on October 11, 2013, and\n697: in particular that the Transaction Committee and CSC had come to an agreement on the remaining open business\n698: points, including the post-signing covenants and the termination fees. Goodwin Procter again reviewed with the\n699: Special Committee its fiduciary duties and provided a summary of the terms of the proposed merger agreement\n700: and the Pamplona capital commitment letter, copies of which were provided to the directors prior to the\n701: meeting. Also at this meeting, BofA Merrill Lynch reviewed with the Special Committee its financial analysis\n702: of the consideration and delivered to the Special Committee an oral opinion, which was confirmed by delivery\n703: of a written opinion dated, October 14, 2013, to the effect that, as of that date and based on and subject to\n704: the assumptions and limitations described in its opinion, the consideration to be received by holders of Mac-\n705: Gray common stock was fair, from a financial point of view, to such holders. Following these presentations,\n706: the Special Committee went into an executive session that excluded BofA Merrill Lynch and, after discussion,\n707: the Special Committee unanimously determined to recommend to the Board that the merger agreement and the\n708: merger were advisable and in the best interests of Mac-Gray's stockholders and that the Board approve the\n709: merger on the terms and subject to the conditions set forth in the merger agreement, adopt the merger\n710: agreement and recommend that the Mac-Gray stockholders adopt and approve the merger agreement. The Special\n711: Committee meeting then adjourned.\n712: Following the adjournment of the Special Committee meeting, a meeting of the Mac-Gray Board of Directors\n713: convened. All members of the Board participated. Representatives from Goodwin Procter led a discussion on the\n714: terms of the merger agreement and advised the Board regarding the likely timing for execution of a definitive\n715: agreement and public announcement of the transaction and a projected closing timetable should the Board\n716: approve the merger. After discussion, the Board (upon the recommendation of the Special Committee) unanimously\n717: determined that the merger agreement and the merger were advisable and in the best interests of Mac-Gray's\n718: stockholders, approved the merger on the terms and subject to the conditions set forth in the merger\n719: agreement, adopted the merger agreement and recommended that the Mac-Gray stockholders adopt and approve the\n720: merger agreement.\n721: Later in the day, on October 14, 2013, the merger agreement was executed, the Pamplona commitment letter was\n722: delivered, Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement and the Mac-Donald voting agreements became\n723: effective.\n724: On October 15, 2013, before the U.S. stock markets opened, Mac-Gray and CSC jointly announced the execution of\n725: the merger agreement.\n726: 41"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 220, \"offset\": 511, \"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/background_wrapped.txt\"}"},