{"type":"text","timestamp":1789824823231,"sessionID":"ses_f462a5515ffeVXejhZ4OL349Hs","part":{"id":"prt_0b9de8236001d26GGfGr0yJuig","sessionID":"ses_f462a5515ffeVXejhZ4OL349Hs","messageID":"msg_0b9ddfdec001rWosPCzthRDEaw","type":"text","text":"Now the main build. First, the ledger data module with all rows, evidence and structured fields:","time":{"start":1789824762422,"end":1789824823231}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824823249,"sessionID":"ses_f462a5515ffeVXejhZ4OL349Hs","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9de82a2001jYTxSipMXHpPoh","sessionID":"ses_f462a5515ffeVXejhZ4OL349Hs","messageID":"msg_0b9ddfdec001rWosPCzthRDEaw","type":"tool","id":"call_00_hBU9qVaDijS223jzcFWz8185","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\"\"\"Ledger rows for the Mac-Gray / CSC-Pamplona deal (worked from the DEFM14A only).\n\nEach row: dict with keys used by build_workbook.py. 'related' references other rows\nby key, resolved to Row ids at build time.\n\"\"\"\n\n# Shorthand for the Conditions detail fixed format\nNN = \"Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: {dd}; Excl: not stated\"\nCOMMITTED = \"Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: {excl}\"\nNOTCOMM = \"Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated\"\n\nROWS = [\ndict(key=\"bofa_prior\", when=\"10/23/2012\", who=\"BofA Merrill Lynch — Mac-Gray (client)\",\n what=\"Adviser engaged\", process=\"1\", round=\"0\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Pre-process context (not a Mac-Gray sale attempt): engaged 10/23/2012 for the 2011-2012 Discussions — Mac-Gray's consideration of a possible acquisition of CSC. CSC was itself sold to Pamplona in May 2013. The mandate was terminated in May 2013 before the sale process (see R006).\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “In connection with Mac-Gray's consideration of a possible acquisition of CSC, which we refer to as the 2011-2012 Discussions, Mac-Gray engaged BofA Merrill Lynch on October 23, 2012.” “During the fall and winter of 2012, CSC engaged in a sale process and, ultimately, CSC was purchased by Pamplona in May 2013.” (both p.27)\",\n source=[\"P-002\"], page=27,\n dfrom=\"2012-10-23\", dto=\"2012-10-23\", wdate=\"2012-10-23\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"bofa_ended\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"apr5\", when=\"04/05/2013\", who=\"Mac-Gray Board of Directors\", what=\"Target sale decision\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"0\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Board discussed CSC's sale to Pamplona and industry M&A activity and authorized Mac-Gray management to work with BofA Merrill Lynch to explore transactional opportunities, including with Party A (a laundry-industry strategic party); further consideration deferred to the May 9 meeting. An exploration authorization, not a commitment to sell.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “the Board discussed the sale of CSC to Pamplona as well as industry-wide merger and acquisition activity and dynamics, and authorized Mac-Gray management to work with BofA Merrill Lynch to explore transactional opportunities that might be available to Mac-Gray, including opportunities with another strategic party, whom we refer to as Party A, in the laundry facilities management industry.” (p.27)\",\n source=[\"P-003\"], page=27,\n dfrom=\"2013-04-05\", dto=\"2013-04-05\", wdate=\"2013-04-05\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"apr8\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"apr8\", when=\"04/08/2013\", who=\"Party A (approached by BofA Merrill Lynch for Mac-Gray)\",\n what=\"Contact\", process=\"1\", round=\"0\", type=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"BofA Merrill Lynch telephoned Party A, as instructed by the Board, to discuss a possible business combination between Party A and Mac-Gray; Party A indicated it might consider one. Direction: Mac-Gray → Party A. First sale-related contact with Party A.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch, as instructed by the Board, telephoned a representative of Party A to discuss generally a possible business combination between Party A and Mac-Gray. During this call, the representative of Party A indicated that Party A might consider a business combination with Mac-Gray.” (p.27)\",\n source=[\"P-004\"], page=27, count=1, review=\"Q1\",\n dfrom=\"2013-04-08\", dto=\"2013-04-08\", wdate=\"2013-04-08\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"a_jun21\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"may9\", when=\"05/09/2013–05/10/2013\", who=\"Mac-Gray Board of Directors; Transaction Committee\",\n what=\"Material process update\", process=\"1\", round=\"0\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Board reviewed strategic alternatives with BofA Merrill Lynch and Goodwin Procter and discussed whether to approach third parties about a potential sale; formed the Transaction Committee (Thomas Bullock and Paul Daoust) to recommend and engage a financial advisor and take administrative actions; deferred the sale-process decision to a later meeting. On 05/10/2013 the Transaction Committee decided to invite three nationally recognized investment banks to submit proposals and recommended that, given his significant family stock ownership and a possible equity rollover, Mr. MacDonald not participate in the Board's evaluation of strategic alternatives or negotiations (he could provide perspectives as requested).\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “the Board formed a transaction committee at this meeting, which we refer to as the Transaction Committee, and appointed Thomas Bullock and Paul Daoust, both independent directors, to serve as its members.” “The Transaction Committee was charged with recommending to the Board the selection and engagement of a financial advisor” (both p.28). “determined to invite three nationally recognized investment banks to submit proposals” (p.28). “Mr. MacDonald should not be permitted to participate in the Board's evaluation of strategic alternatives or any negotiations with any interested parties in a sale process” (p.28)\",\n source=[\"P-005\", \"P-006\", \"P-007\", \"P-008\"], page=28,\n dfrom=\"2013-05-09\", dto=\"2013-05-10\", wdate=\"2013-05-09\", dbasis=\"Reported interval\", dmethod=\"Assigned: midpoint\",\n related=[\"bofa_new\", \"jun12\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"goodwin\", when=\"05/09/2013 (earliest observed service; commencement not disclosed)\",\n who=\"Goodwin Procter LLP — Mac-Gray (client)\", what=\"Adviser service observed\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"0\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray; first observed advising the Board at the 05/09/2013 Board meeting, then the Transaction Committee and Special Committee through signing (fiduciary reviews, process and agreement negotiation). Engagement or selection date not disclosed in the filing; no adviser row for a later re-engagement.\",\n evidence=\"Stated (service; no engagement date). “at an in-person meeting of the Board on April 5, 2013, ... representatives from BofA Merrill Lynch and Goodwin Procter LLP, outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray, were also in attendance” — first narrative mention in the background is the May 9, 2013 meeting (p.27–28). The filing does not state an engagement date; service observed from 05/09/2013.\",\n source=[\"P-005\"], page=28,\n dfrom=\"2013-05-09\", dto=\"\", wdate=\"2013-05-09\", dbasis=\"Relative only\", dmethod=\"Assigned: bound\",\n related=[\"bofa_new\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"bofa_ended\", when=\"05/14/2013–05/15/2013 (committee decision 05/14; letter sent 05/15)\",\n who=\"Transaction Committee / BofA Merrill Lynch\", what=\"Adviser ended\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"0\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Transaction Committee determined to terminate BofA Merrill Lynch's engagement letter entered for the 2011-2012 Discussions; Mac-Gray sent the termination letter 05/15/2013. Reason disclosed: BofA was one of the banks invited to submit a proposal for the new mandate and the CSC sale process had ended.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “Given that BofA Merrill Lynch was one of the investment banks to be invited to submit a proposal and that the CSC sale process had ended, the Transaction Committee determined to terminate BofA Merrill Lynch's engagement letter entered into for purposes of the 2011-2012 Discussions.” “On May 15, 2013, Mac-Gray sent a letter to BofA Merrill Lynch terminating their engagement in connection with the 2011-2012 Discussions.” (both p.29)\",\n source=[\"P-009\", \"P-010\"], page=29,\n dfrom=\"2013-05-14\", dto=\"2013-05-15\", wdate=\"2013-05-14\", dbasis=\"Reported interval\", dmethod=\"Assigned: bound\",\n related=[\"bofa_prior\", \"bofa_new\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"bofa_new\", when=\"05/30/2013–05/31/2013 (Board approval 05/30; engagement letter 05/31)\",\n who=\"BofA Merrill Lynch — Mac-Gray (client)\", what=\"Adviser engaged\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"0\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Board unanimously approved engaging BofA Merrill Lynch as Mac-Gray's financial advisor for the strategic-alternatives review and potential sale process; BofA had presented 05/22/2013, the other two invited candidates 05/29/2013. Engagement letter entered 05/31/2013; BofA agreed not to act as a source of new acquisition financing for potential buyers without Mac-Gray's prior written consent. BofA advised through signing and delivered its written fairness opinion dated 10/14/2013; its fee includes a portion payable on the opinion and a significant portion contingent on consummation.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “Based on the recommendation of the Transaction Committee, the Board unanimously approved the engagement of BofA Merrill Lynch on the terms discussed at this meeting.” (p.29) “On May 31, 2013, Mac-Gray entered into an engagement letter with BofA Merrill Lynch with respect to the Board's undertaking a review of strategic alternatives, including a potential sale process, and in which BofA Merrill Lynch agreed not to engage as a possible source of new acquisition financing for any potential buyers in connection with any such sale process without Mac-Gray's prior written consent.” (p.30) “We have acted as financial advisor to MGC in connection with the Merger and will receive a fee for our services, a portion of which is payable upon the rendering of this opinion and a significant portion of which is contingent upon consummation of the Merger.” (Annex B, p. B-2)\",\n source=[\"P-011\", \"P-012\", \"P-013\", \"P-014\", \"P-016\", \"X-028\"], page=30,\n dfrom=\"2013-05-30\", dto=\"2013-05-31\", wdate=\"2013-05-30\", dbasis=\"Reported interval\", dmethod=\"Assigned: bound\",\n related=[\"bofa_ended\", \"signed\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"moab_proxy\", when=\"05/30/2013\", who=\"Moab / Mac-Gray annual stockholder meeting\",\n what=\"Activist involvement\", process=\"1\", round=\"0\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Moab-nominated candidates Michael M. Rothenberg (Moab co-founder and General Partner) and James E. Hyman were elected as directors in place of two incumbent nominees after a proxy contest; board size was reduced to seven. Context: the board change led to Mr. Rothenberg's exclusion from the sale process given Moab's possible equity rollover interest; Moab held approximately 9% (06/12/2013).\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “Mac-Gray and Moab engaged in a proxy contest leading up to the annual meeting and Mr. Rothenberg and Mr. Hyman were elected in place of Mac-Gray's incumbent nominees, David W. Bryan and Mary Ann Tocio.” “Mr. Rothenberg is a co-founder and the General Partner of Moab” (both p.29). “At the time of this meeting, Moab beneficially owned approximately 9% of Mac-Gray's outstanding common stock.” (p.30)\",\n source=[\"P-015\", \"P-017\"], page=29,\n dfrom=\"2013-05-30\", dto=\"2013-05-30\", wdate=\"2013-05-30\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"jun12\", \"moab_denied\", \"moab_resolved\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"jun12\", when=\"06/12/2013\", who=\"Mac-Gray / new directors (Rothenberg, Hyman)\",\n what=\"Material process update\", process=\"1\", round=\"0\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Orientation of new directors: each received an overview of the strategic-alternatives review and potential sale process; with Mr. Rothenberg the participants discussed that if Moab might want an equity rollover in a sale transaction resulting from the process, he would need to be excluded from the process from the outset. Moab then held approximately 9% of Mac-Gray's outstanding stock.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “to the extent Moab might have an interest in an equity rollover of all or a portion of Moab's shares of Mac-Gray common stock in connection with any sale transaction that might result from the Board's strategic alternatives process, Mr. Rothenberg would need to be excluded from the process from the outset. At the time of this meeting, Moab beneficially owned approximately 9% of Mac-Gray's outstanding common stock.” (p.30)\",\n source=[\"P-017\"], page=30,\n dfrom=\"2013-06-12\", dto=\"2013-06-12\", wdate=\"2013-06-12\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"moab_proxy\", \"r1_open\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"a_jun21\", when=\"06/21/2013\", who=\"Party A\", what=\"Bid\", process=\"1\", round=\"0\", type=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"Unsolicited proposal to the Board for a whole-company acquisition at an all-cash price of $17.00–$19.00 per share. Made before any substantive diligence access (no confidentiality agreement yet; Party A's NDA was executed 08/05/2013), so Heavy by context. Still standing when round 1 was evaluated (reviewed with the three preliminary indications at the 07/25/2013 Special Committee meeting).\",\n formality=\"Informal\", cond=\"Heavy\",\n evidence=\"Stated (price). “On June 21, 2013, Party A submitted an unsolicited proposal to the Mac-Gray Board of Directors offering to purchase Mac-Gray for an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $19.00 per share” (p.30). Context: no substantive access before the proposal — “outside counsel to Party A and representatives of Goodwin Procter negotiated the terms of a confidentiality and standstill agreement, but did not come to agreement on the terms of the customer and employee non-solicitation provisions” between 07/11 and 07/23 (P-030, p.33); reviewed as still standing on 07/25/2013 (P-033, p.33).\",\n source=[\"P-018\", \"P-030\", \"P-033\"], page=30, count=1, review=\"Q1; Q5\",\n plow=17.00, phigh=19.00, pkind=\"Bidder range\", porigin=\"Stated\", currency=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=\"\",\n conddetail=NN.format(dd=\"no\"),\n dfrom=\"2013-06-21\", dto=\"2013-06-21\", wdate=\"2013-06-21\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"apr8\", \"r1_open\", \"a_sep10\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"r1_open\", when=\"06/24/2013\", who=\"Mac-Gray Board of Directors / Special Committee\",\n what=\"Round opened\", process=\"1\", round=\"1\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"R1 anchor: 06/24/2013 Special Committee determination to commence the sale process and approach 50 parties (15 strategic, 35 financial) — first outreach executed within days (contacts reported 06/28/2013). Rejected anchor candidates: R003 (04/08/2013 single Party A contact) and R009 (06/21/2013 unsolicited Party A proposal). The Board also excluded Mr. MacDonald and Mr. Rothenberg from evaluating strategic alternatives (possible rollovers) and established the Special Committee (Bullock chair; Daoust, Hyman, Meagher, Percelay, Robinson). Deadline set: preliminary indications of interest due 07/23/2013 (informational package issued to NDA signers). Round finality: Not final — initial solicitation for preliminary indications; no finality signal.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “the Special Committee concluded that it would be in the best interests of stockholders to consider a potential sale of Mac-Gray” (p.31). “the Board decided, and Mr. MacDonald and Mr. Rothenberg agreed, that it would be appropriate to exclude Mr. MacDonald and Mr. Rothenberg from the Board's evaluation of strategic alternatives and any negotiations with third parties that might take place” (p.30). “a total of 50 parties, including CSC and Pamplona, who together we refer to as CSC/Pamplona, and Party A, to solicit potential interest in a transaction with Mac-Gray, 15 of which were potential strategic buyers and 35 of which were potential financial buyers, including private equity firms” (p.32). “furnished an informational package for the purpose of providing potential bidders with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest, which they were instructed to submit by July 23, 2013” (p.32)\",\n source=[\"P-019\", \"P-021\", \"P-022\", \"P-023\"], page=31, due=\"2013-07-23\", rfinal=\"Not final\", review=\"Q1\",\n dfrom=\"2013-06-24\", dto=\"2013-06-24\", wdate=\"2013-06-24\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"a_jun21\", \"apr8\", \"contact_strat\", \"dl_jul23\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"contact_strat\", when=\"late June 2013 (after the 06/24/2013 decision; contacts reported by 06/28/2013)\",\n who=\"BofA Merrill Lynch (for Mac-Gray) — strategic parties\", what=\"Contact\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"1\", type=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"Outreach wave to the 15 potential strategic buyers identified at the 06/24/2013 meeting, including Party A and CSC/Pamplona; Party A was already in contact from 04/08/2013. Part of the 50-party universe; 2 of the 15 (Party A, CSC/Pamplona) ultimately executed confidentiality agreements.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “BofA Merrill Lynch contacted the strategic and financial parties identified at the June 24th Special Committee meeting” (p.32); “a total of 50 parties, ... 15 of which were potential strategic buyers and 35 of which were potential financial buyers” (p.32); “including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona)” signed confidentiality agreements (p.32).\",\n source=[\"P-022\", \"P-023\"], page=32, count=15,\n dfrom=\"2013-06-24\", dto=\"\", wdate=\"2013-06-24\", dbasis=\"Relative only\", dmethod=\"Assigned: bound\",\n related=[\"r1_open\", \"apr8\", \"contact_fin\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"contact_fin\", when=\"late June 2013 (after the 06/24/2013 decision; contacts reported by 06/28/2013)\",\n who=\"BofA Merrill Lynch (for Mac-Gray) — financial parties\", what=\"Contact\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"1\", type=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Outreach wave to the 35 potential financial buyers identified at the 06/24/2013 meeting, including private equity firms (among them Party B and Party C); 18 of the 35 ultimately executed confidentiality agreements (including Party B and Party C).\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “BofA Merrill Lynch contacted the strategic and financial parties identified at the June 24th Special Committee meeting” (p.32); “35 of which were potential financial buyers, including private equity firms”; “18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C)” signed confidentiality agreements (p.32).\",\n source=[\"P-022\", \"P-023\"], page=32, count=35,\n dfrom=\"2013-06-24\", dto=\"\", wdate=\"2013-06-24\", dbasis=\"Relative only\", dmethod=\"Assigned: bound\",\n related=[\"r1_open\", \"contact_strat\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"resid_nda\", when=\"late June–August 2013 (two-month signing window; dates not individually disclosed)\",\n who=\"16 residual financial NDA signers\", what=\"NDA signed\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"1\", type=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Residual cohort: 18 financial NDA signers less the two individually recorded financial signers (Party B, Party C) = 16 financial NDA signers. The filing reports the 20 signers collectively over a two-month window and does not date them; the two strategic signers (Party A, CSC/Pamplona) are recorded individually. Agreements were on a form provided by Mac-Gray, individually negotiated but not materially varied; they included standstill provisions with sunset rights to make confidential proposals on announcement of a business combination. Working date is the first day of the reported signing window (display convention) — not an observed signing date. Count 16.\",\n evidence=\"Stated (population and window). “Over the next two months a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C), entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray on a form provided by Mac-Gray, the terms of which were individually negotiated with potential bidders, but did not vary materially from the form provided.” “The confidentiality agreements contained customary non-disclosure provisions and a customary standstill provision that either expired or permitted the potential bidder to make confidential proposals to Mac-Gray (a so-called \"sunset\" provision) upon announcement of a business combination between Mac-Gray and a third party” (both p.32).\",\n source=[\"P-023\"], page=32, count=16, review=\"Q3; Q7\",\n dfrom=\"2013-06-24\", dto=\"2013-08-31\", wdate=\"2013-06-24\", dbasis=\"Approximate window\", dmethod=\"Assigned: bound\",\n related=[\"resid_nosub\", \"b_nda\", \"c_nda\", \"csc_nda\", \"a_nda\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"b_nda\", when=\"06/28/2013\", who=\"Party B\", what=\"NDA signed\", process=\"1\", round=\"1\", type=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Party B entered a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided the informational package (preliminary indication of interest due 07/23/2013). First observed participation by Party B.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “Later on June 28, 2013, Party B, entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package for the purpose of providing Party B with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest.” (p.32)\",\n source=[\"P-025\"], page=32, count=1, review=\"Q3\",\n dfrom=\"2013-06-28\", dto=\"2013-06-28\", wdate=\"2013-06-28\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"b_jul24\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"c_nda\", when=\"06/30/2013\", who=\"Party C\", what=\"NDA signed\", process=\"1\", round=\"1\", type=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Party C entered a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided the informational package (preliminary indication of interest due 07/23/2013). First observed participation by Party C.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “On June 30, 2013, Party C entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package for the purpose of providing Party C with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest.” (p.32)\",\n source=[\"P-026\"], page=32, count=1, review=\"Q3\",\n dfrom=\"2013-06-30\", dto=\"2013-06-30\", wdate=\"2013-06-30\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"c_jul24\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"moab_denied\", when=\"07/06/2013\", who=\"Special Committee / Moab / CSC/Pamplona\",\n what=\"Material process update\", process=\"1\", round=\"1\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Rollover (step 1 — exclusivity denied): the Special Committee denied the request that Moab be permitted to partner exclusively with CSC/Pamplona (including sharing under CSC/Pamplona's confidentiality agreement), so that Moab's potential equity rollover remained available as a source of capital for other bidders; the Committee told the parties it was premature and that rollover discussions would be permitted at a later stage. Mr. Rothenberg had raised Moab's interest with Goodwin Procter on 07/03/2013.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “the Special Committee decided to deny the exclusivity request at this stage of the process so that the potential equity rollover of Moab's shares could be available as a source of capital for other potential bidders. The Special Committee instructed BofA Merrill Lynch and Goodwin Procter to communicate to CSC/Pamplona and Mr. Rothenberg, respectively, that it was premature for Mac-Gray to permit Moab to engage in equity rollover discussions with any party, including CSC/Pamplona, but that such discussions would be permitted at a later stage of the sale process.” (p.32–33)\",\n source=[\"P-027\", \"P-028\"], page=32,\n dfrom=\"2013-07-06\", dto=\"2013-07-06\", wdate=\"2013-07-06\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"moab_proxy\", \"moab_resolved\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"csc_nda\", when=\"07/11/2013\", who=\"CSC/Pamplona\", what=\"NDA signed\", process=\"1\", round=\"1\", type=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"CSC/Pamplona entered a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided the informational package. The merger agreement later confirms the July 11, 2013 confidentiality letter agreement among Pamplona Capital Management LLC, Parent and Mac-Gray.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “On July 11, 2013, CSC/Pamplona entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and were provided with an informational package for the purpose of providing CSC/Pamplona with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest.” (p.33) “Parent and the Company hereby acknowledge and agree that they are and shall continue to be bound by that certain letter agreement dated as of July 11, 2013, among Pamplona Capital Management LLC, Parent and the Company (the \"Confidentiality Agreement\").” (Annex A, Section 6.17, p. A-46)\",\n source=[\"P-029\", \"X-027\"], page=33, count=1, review=\"Q3\",\n dfrom=\"2013-07-11\", dto=\"2013-07-11\", wdate=\"2013-07-11\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"csc_jul23\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"dl_jul23\", when=\"07/23/2013 (scheduled due date for preliminary indications)\",\n who=\"NDA signers (solicitation deadline)\", what=\"Deadline\", process=\"1\", round=\"1\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Preliminary indications of interest were due 07/23/2013 (deadline set with the launch of the process; see R010). CSC/Pamplona submitted on the due date; Party B (07/24) and Party C (07/24–25) submitted after it and were considered (late bids accepted). No extension is disclosed.\",\n evidence=\"Stated (due date reached and operative). “furnished an informational package for the purpose of providing potential bidders with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest, which they were instructed to submit by July 23, 2013” (p.32); submissions and later consideration documented at P-031, P-032, P-033, P-035.\",\n source=[\"P-023\", \"P-031\", \"P-032\", \"P-033\", \"P-035\"], page=32, due=\"2013-07-23\",\n dltreatment=\"Late bids accepted\", review=\"Q2\",\n dfrom=\"2013-07-23\", dto=\"2013-07-23\", wdate=\"2013-07-23\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"r1_open\", \"csc_jul23\", \"resid_nosub\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"csc_jul23\", when=\"07/23/2013\", who=\"CSC/Pamplona\", what=\"Bid\", process=\"1\", round=\"1\", type=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"Preliminary indication of interest, all-cash $18.50 per share, submitted on the 07/23/2013 deadline. First bid by CSC/Pamplona (NDA 07/11/2013; preliminary review only — no substantive data-site or management access yet, so Heavy by context).\",\n formality=\"Informal\", cond=\"Heavy\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “On July 23, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share.” (p.33) Context: “Between July 11, 2013 and July 23, 2013, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona engaged in a preliminary review of Mac-Gray and the potential acquisition opportunity.” (p.33); management presentations and data-site access came later (P-042, p.34).\",\n source=[\"P-031\", \"P-030\", \"P-042\"], page=33, count=1, review=\"Q5\",\n plow=18.50, phigh=18.50, pkind=\"Point\", porigin=\"Stated\", currency=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=18.50,\n conddetail=NN.format(dd=\"yes\"),\n dfrom=\"2013-07-23\", dto=\"2013-07-23\", wdate=\"2013-07-23\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"csc_nda\", \"csc_sep9\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"resid_nosub\", when=\"by 07/23/2013\", who=\"16 residual financial NDA signers\", what=\"Did not submit\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"1\", type=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Inferred: residual — 20 NDA signers (2 strategic + 18 financial) − 4 individually recorded participants (Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona) = 16 residual financial signers with no preliminary indication of interest submitted by the 07/23/2013 deadline; the filing names no other submitters, and the 07/25/2013 Special Committee review addressed only Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona and the standing Party A proposal. Base assumes the residual signers had signed by and were eligible for the solicitation; the filing dates their signatures only as a two-month window. No motive, identity or voluntary withdrawal inferred.\",\n evidence=\"Inferred: residual. “a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C), entered into confidentiality agreements” (P-023, p.32); “representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch reviewed the preliminary indications of interest received from Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona as well as the Party A June 21 proposal” (P-033, p.33). Arithmetic: 20 − 4 = 16.\",\n source=[\"P-023\", \"P-033\"], page=33, count=16, review=\"Q3; Q4\",\n decidedby=\"Unknown\", exitreason=\"Not stated\", obasis=\"Inferred: residual\",\n dfrom=\"\", dto=\"2013-07-23\", wdate=\"2013-07-23\", dbasis=\"Relative only\", dmethod=\"Assigned: deadline\",\n related=[\"resid_nda\", \"dl_jul23\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"b_jul24\", when=\"07/24/2013 (one day after the 07/23/2013 due date)\", who=\"Party B\", what=\"Bid\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"1\", type=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Preliminary indication of interest, all-cash $17.00–$18.00 per share, submitted after the 07/23/2013 due date and considered at the 07/25/2013 Special Committee meeting (late bid accepted). Preliminary review only; Heavy by context.\",\n formality=\"Informal\", cond=\"Heavy\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “On July 24, 2013, Party B submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $18.00 per share.” (p.33) Considered: “reviewed the preliminary indications of interest received from Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona” (p.33).\",\n source=[\"P-032\", \"P-033\"], page=33, count=1, review=\"Q2; Q5\",\n plow=17.00, phigh=18.00, pkind=\"Bidder range\", porigin=\"Stated\", currency=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=\"\",\n conddetail=NN.format(dd=\"yes\"),\n dfrom=\"2013-07-24\", dto=\"2013-07-24\", wdate=\"2013-07-24\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"b_nda\", \"b_sep9\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"c_jul24\", when=\"07/24/2013–07/25/2013 (oral indication 07/24; written indication 07/25)\",\n who=\"Party C\", what=\"Bid\", process=\"1\", round=\"1\", type=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Oral preliminary indication of interest 07/24/2013 at $15.00–$17.00 per share, followed by a written indication of interest 07/25/2013 at $16.00–$16.50 per share; treated as one bid (an IOI and its written offer are one submission). The written indication came after the 07/23/2013 due date and was considered (late bid accepted). Preliminary review only; Heavy by context.\",\n formality=\"Informal\", cond=\"Heavy\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “representatives from Party C called BofA Merrill Lynch and presented an oral preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $15.00 to $17.00 per share” (p.33). “Later on July 25, 2013, Party C submitted a written indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $16.50 per share.” (p.34) Considered at the 07/25/2013 Special Committee meeting (P-033, p.33).\",\n source=[\"P-032\", \"P-033\", \"P-035\"], page=34, count=1, review=\"Q2; Q5; Q7\",\n plow=16.00, phigh=16.50, pkind=\"Bidder range\", porigin=\"Stated\", currency=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=\"\",\n conddetail=NN.format(dd=\"yes\"),\n dfrom=\"2013-07-24\", dto=\"2013-07-25\", wdate=\"2013-07-24\", dbasis=\"Reported interval\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"c_nda\", \"c_sep10\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"r2_open\", when=\"07/25/2013\", who=\"Special Committee\", what=\"Round opened\", process=\"1\", round=\"2\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Round 2 opened: Special Committee reviewed the three preliminary indications (Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona) and the still-standing Party A June 21 proposal; indications were lower than expected; adopted staged disclosure of sensitive information for the second stage. Authorized BofA to arrange management presentations and high-level information access with the four interested bidders (Party A conditional on executing its NDA; synergies discussions for Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and thereafter to request revised indications. Mr. Rothenberg to recuse himself for the duration of the process (continuing rollover interest). Round finality: Not final — revised written proposals were sought only to continue in the process; no finality signal. Round-2 bidders: Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona (4 units).\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “the Special Committee concluded that it would be advisable to stage the disclosure of such information to each of the bidders to the extent that a bidder's indication of interest and other actions demonstrated its seriousness in acquiring Mac-Gray on terms viewed favorably by the Special Committee.” “the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure as discussed at this meeting and to reach out to each of the four interested bidders and arrange management meetings” (both p.33–34). “decided that Mr. Rothenberg should be asked to recuse himself from participating in Board meetings for the duration of the sale process” (p.33).\",\n source=[\"P-033\", \"P-034\"], page=34, rfinal=\"Not final\", review=\"Q1\",\n dfrom=\"2013-07-25\", dto=\"2013-07-25\", wdate=\"2013-07-25\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"r1_open\", \"a_nda\", \"info_access\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"a_nda\", when=\"08/05/2013 (negotiations from 07/11–07/23; resumed 07/27)\", who=\"Party A\",\n what=\"NDA signed\", process=\"1\", round=\"2\", type=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"Party A entered a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and received the informational package to potentially improve its June 21 proposal. Non-solicitation terms were agreed with the Transaction Committee on 07/27/2013 (the filing prints “July 27, 2103” — a typo retained; the supported reading is 07/27/2013). Party A's standing round-0 proposal remained under consideration.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “Discussions with Party A resumed on July 27, 2103 and Party A and the Transaction Committee agreed to the terms of the customer and employee non-solicitation provisions. On August 5, 2013, Party A entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package for the purpose of providing Party A with data to potentially improve the terms of the Party A June 21 proposal.” (p.34) Wording of the source typo preserved; proposed corrected date 07/27/2013 (see Q7).\",\n source=[\"P-030\", \"P-036\"], page=34, count=1, review=\"Q3; Q7\",\n dfrom=\"2013-08-05\", dto=\"2013-08-05\", wdate=\"2013-08-05\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"a_jun21\", \"info_access\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"info_access\", when=\"08/06/2013–08/27/2013 (staged access during diligence)\",\n who=\"Mac-Gray/BofA Merrill Lynch → Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona\",\n what=\"Information access changed\", process=\"1\", round=\"2\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Differentiated, staged access among the four live bidders: Party B and Party C (financial bidders) received broad access to the electronic data site; Party A and CSC/Pamplona (strategic bidders) received somewhat limited access, with customer data (including locations) reserved until later in the process. Stated rationale: risk of misuse of sensitive competitive information by strategic bidders (07/25/2013 staging decision). Management presentations were held for each advanced bidder (B 08/06; C 08/08; CSC/Pamplona 08/12; A 08/14); Party A and CSC/Pamplona also held synergies discussions with management.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “Party B and Party C, in light of the fact that they were financial bidders, were given broad access to an electronic data site, and Party A and CSC/Pamplona, in light of the fact that they were strategic bidders, were given somewhat limited access to this electronic data site, with access to customer data, including customer locations, being reserved until later in the process as part of the staging discussed at the July 25th Special Committee meeting.” “both Party A and CSC/Pamplona participated in discussions with members of Mac-Gray management around synergies.” (both p.34) Presentations at P-037–P-040 (p.34).\",\n source=[\"P-033\", \"P-034\", \"P-037\", \"P-038\", \"P-039\", \"P-040\", \"P-041\", \"P-042\"], page=34,\n dfrom=\"2013-08-06\", dto=\"2013-08-27\", wdate=\"2013-08-06\", dbasis=\"Reported interval\", dmethod=\"Assigned: bound\",\n related=[\"r2_open\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"dlset_sep9\", when=\"08/27/2013\", who=\"BofA Merrill Lynch (for the Special Committee)\",\n what=\"Deadline set\", process=\"1\", round=\"2\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Following the 08/15/2013 Special Committee authorization, BofA sent a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona requesting revised written proposals no later than 09/09/2013 to continue in the process and pursue in-depth confirmatory diligence; the letter asked for valuation, financing sources/structure, regulatory approvals, post-signing covenants and diligence focus areas.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “BofA Merrill Lynch, as instructed by the Special Committee, sent a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013 if such bidders wished to proceed further in the process to pursue an in-depth evaluation of Mac-Gray with the objective of making a revised offer.” (p.35) Authorization: “the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to send a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona once all four of the bidders' due diligence was substantially complete requesting that ... such party submit a revised written proposal in order to continue in the process” (p.34).\",\n source=[\"P-041\", \"P-043\"], page=35, due=\"2013-09-09\", review=\"Q2\",\n dfrom=\"2013-08-27\", dto=\"2013-08-27\", wdate=\"2013-08-27\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"dl_sep9\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"dl_sep9\", when=\"09/09/2013 (scheduled due date for revised written proposals)\",\n who=\"Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona (solicitation deadline)\", what=\"Deadline\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"2\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Revised written proposals were due 09/09/2013. CSC/Pamplona and Party B submitted on the due date; Party A and Party C submitted on 09/10/2013 and were considered at the 09/11/2013 Special Committee meeting (late bids accepted; no extension disclosed).\",\n evidence=\"Stated (due date reached and operative). “instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013” (p.35); submissions at P-047 and P-048; considered: “the Special Committee held a telephonic meeting to review the revised indications of interest submitted by Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona” on 09/11/2013 (P-050, p.35).\",\n source=[\"P-043\", \"P-047\", \"P-048\", \"P-050\"], page=35, due=\"2013-09-09\",\n dltreatment=\"Late bids accepted\", review=\"Q2\",\n dfrom=\"2013-09-09\", dto=\"2013-09-09\", wdate=\"2013-09-09\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"dlset_sep9\", \"csc_sep9\", \"b_sep9\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"csc_sep9\", when=\"09/09/2013\", who=\"CSC/Pamplona\", what=\"Bid\", process=\"1\", round=\"2\", type=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"Revised indication of interest: all-cash $19.50 per share; Pamplona committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction; requested two weeks of exclusive negotiations. Light: committed financing, no diligence condition reported (exclusivity request does not change the level).\",\n formality=\"Informal\", cond=\"Light\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “On September 9, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $19.50 per share, indicating that Pamplona was committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction and requesting that CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray agree to exclusive negotiations for two weeks.” (p.35)\",\n source=[\"P-047\"], page=35, count=1, review=\"Q5\",\n plow=19.50, phigh=19.50, pkind=\"Point\", porigin=\"Stated\", currency=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=19.50,\n conddetail=COMMITTED.format(excl=\"requested (2 wks)\"),\n dfrom=\"2013-09-09\", dto=\"2013-09-09\", wdate=\"2013-09-09\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"csc_jul23\", \"csc_sep18\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"b_sep9\", when=\"09/09/2013\", who=\"Party B\", what=\"Bid\", process=\"1\", round=\"2\", type=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Revised indication of interest: all-cash $18.50 per share; proposed financing from a combination of affiliated-fund equity and third-party debt; no firm financing commitment (stated) — Heavy.\",\n formality=\"Informal\", cond=\"Heavy\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share and proposed to finance the transaction with a combination of equity from affiliated funds and third party debt. Party B's revised indication of interest did not include a firm financing commitment.” (p.35)\",\n source=[\"P-047\"], page=35, count=1, review=\"Q5\",\n plow=18.50, phigh=18.50, pkind=\"Point\", porigin=\"Stated\", currency=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=18.50,\n conddetail=NOTCOMM,\n dfrom=\"2013-09-09\", dto=\"2013-09-09\", wdate=\"2013-09-09\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"b_jul24\", \"b_sep18\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"a_sep10\", when=\"09/10/2013\", who=\"Party A\", what=\"Bid\", process=\"1\", round=\"2\", type=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"Revised indication of interest: all-cash $18.00–$19.00 per share, to be financed by outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity sources; no firm financing commitment (stated) — Heavy.\",\n formality=\"Informal\", cond=\"Heavy\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “On September 10, 2013, Party A submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share, to be financed by outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity sources.” “Neither Party A's nor Party C's revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment.” (both p.35)\",\n source=[\"P-048\"], page=35, count=1, review=\"Q5\",\n plow=18.00, phigh=19.00, pkind=\"Bidder range\", porigin=\"Stated\", currency=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=\"\",\n conddetail=NOTCOMM,\n dfrom=\"2013-09-10\", dto=\"2013-09-10\", wdate=\"2013-09-10\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"a_jun21\", \"a_reaff\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"c_sep10\", when=\"09/10/2013\", who=\"Party C\", what=\"Bid\", process=\"1\", round=\"2\", type=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Revised oral indication of interest (telephone call to BofA Merrill Lynch): all-cash $16.00–$17.00 per share; no firm financing commitment (stated) — Heavy.\",\n formality=\"Informal\", cond=\"Heavy\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch, a representative of Party C indicated that it was submitting a revised oral indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share. Neither Party A's nor Party C's revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment.” (p.35)\",\n source=[\"P-048\"], page=35, count=1, review=\"Q5\",\n plow=16.00, phigh=17.00, pkind=\"Bidder range\", porigin=\"Stated\", currency=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=\"\",\n conddetail=NOTCOMM,\n dfrom=\"2013-09-10\", dto=\"2013-09-10\", wdate=\"2013-09-10\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"c_jul24\", \"c_nosub\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"macd_decline\", when=\"09/11/2013\", who=\"Transaction Committee → Mr. MacDonald (rollover)\",\n what=\"Material process update\", process=\"1\", round=\"2\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Rollover (declined): the Transaction Committee gave Mr. MacDonald, without identifying bidders or prices, a limited overview of the process status so he could consider whether he remained interested in a possible rollover of his Mac-Gray shares; he stated he had decided he was not interested in rolling over any shares in any transaction.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “provided Mr. MacDonald with a limited overview of the status of the Special Committee's review of strategic alternatives ... so that Mr. MacDonald could consider whether he continued to have an interest in potentially rolling over any of his Mac-Gray shares in a transaction. During this call, Mr. MacDonald indicated that he had decided that he was not interested in rolling over any of his shares in any transaction.” (p.35)\",\n source=[\"P-049\"], page=35,\n dfrom=\"2013-09-11\", dto=\"2013-09-11\", wdate=\"2013-09-11\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"r3_open\", \"macd_brief\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"r3_open\", when=\"09/11/2013\", who=\"Special Committee\", what=\"Round opened\", process=\"1\", round=\"3\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Round 3 opened: after BofA reported it was unlikely any bidder would proceed without Mr. MacDonald's express support and the Committee agreed his perspective on price was critical, the Special Committee instructed BofA to call Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona to request final indications of interest by 09/18/2013 and to indicate that Mac-Gray would consider a short period of exclusive negotiations with one bidder depending on price and deal certainty. Deadline set: final indications due 09/18/2013. Round finality: Announced as final — bidders were told this was the final indications stage. Round-3 bidders: Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona (4 invited).\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “the Special Committee instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to call each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013 and to indicate that Mac-Gray would consider engaging in a short period of exclusive negotiations with one of the bidders depending upon, among other things, the proposed purchase price and the level of deal certainty indicated in the bidder's final proposal.” “any potential acquiror would be unlikely to proceed without knowing that Mr. MacDonald would support the transaction.” (both p.36)\",\n source=[\"P-050\"], page=36, due=\"2013-09-18\", rfinal=\"Announced as final\", review=\"Q1\",\n dfrom=\"2013-09-11\", dto=\"2013-09-11\", wdate=\"2013-09-11\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"macd_decline\", \"macd_brief\", \"dl_sep18\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"macd_brief\", when=\"09/12/2013\", who=\"BofA Merrill Lynch → Mr. MacDonald\",\n what=\"Material process update\", process=\"1\", round=\"3\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Mr. MacDonald received a detailed overview of the process, the status of negotiations and the identities of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona; he voiced general support for continuing the process but expressed the view that Mac-Gray should continue to seek a higher value for stockholders.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch participated in a telephone conference call with Mr. MacDonald and provided him with a detailed overview of the strategic alternatives process, including the status of negotiations with and the identity of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona. Although Mr. MacDonald voiced his general support for continuing with the process, he expressed his view that Mac-Gray should continue to seek a higher value for stockholders.” (p.36)\",\n source=[\"P-051\"], page=36,\n dfrom=\"2013-09-12\", dto=\"2013-09-12\", wdate=\"2013-09-12\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"r3_open\", \"sep19_decision\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"dl_sep18\", when=\"09/18/2013 (scheduled due date for final indications)\",\n who=\"Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona (solicitation deadline)\", what=\"Deadline\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"3\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Final indications of interest were due 09/18/2013. CSC/Pamplona and Party B submitted, Party A reiterated its prior offer, and Party C did not submit. The Special Committee evaluated the proposals on 09/19/2013 (enforced: the date passed with no extension and the target took its next step on the bids in hand).\",\n evidence=\"Stated (due date reached and operative). “request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013” (p.36); submissions and evaluation at P-053 and P-054. No extension disclosed; selection followed 09/19/2013 (P-055, p.37).\",\n source=[\"P-050\", \"P-053\", \"P-054\", \"P-055\"], page=36, due=\"2013-09-18\",\n dltreatment=\"Enforced\", review=\"Q2\",\n dfrom=\"2013-09-18\", dto=\"2013-09-18\", wdate=\"2013-09-18\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"r3_open\", \"csc_sep18\", \"c_nosub\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"csc_sep18\", when=\"09/18/2013\", who=\"CSC/Pamplona\", what=\"Bid\", process=\"1\", round=\"3\", type=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"Final-round proposal: all-cash $20.75 per share; Pamplona committed to provide 100% of the capital required; requested two weeks of exclusive negotiations. Formal as a response on the requested basis to the target's final-indications solicitation (signal 2). Light: committed financing and no diligence condition reported.\",\n formality=\"Formal\", cond=\"Light\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “On September 18, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share, reiterating that Pamplona was committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction and requesting that CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray agree to engage in exclusive negotiations for two weeks.” (p.36) Final solicitation: “request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013” (P-050, p.36).\",\n source=[\"P-053\", \"P-050\"], page=36, count=1, review=\"Q5\",\n plow=20.75, phigh=20.75, pkind=\"Point\", porigin=\"Stated\", currency=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=20.75,\n conddetail=COMMITTED.format(excl=\"requested (2 wks)\"),\n dfrom=\"2013-09-18\", dto=\"2013-09-18\", wdate=\"2013-09-18\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"csc_sep9\", \"sep19_decision\", \"csc_sep21\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"a_reaff\", when=\"09/18/2013\", who=\"Party A\", what=\"Bid reaffirmed\", process=\"1\", round=\"3\", type=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"Party A reiterated by telephone that its previous $18.00–$19.00 all-cash indication was its best and final offer; no new price. Formal as a supported best-and-final response to the target's final-indications solicitation (signal 2). Heavy: no firm financing commitment was ever reported.\",\n formality=\"Formal\", cond=\"Heavy\",\n evidence=\"Stated (reaffirmation). “Party A reiterated in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer.” (p.36) Financing position carried: “Neither Party A's nor Party C's revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment.” (P-048, p.35)\",\n source=[\"P-053\", \"P-048\"], page=36, count=1, review=\"Q5\",\n plow=18.00, phigh=19.00, pkind=\"Bidder range\", porigin=\"Carried forward\", currency=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=\"\",\n conddetail=NOTCOMM,\n dfrom=\"2013-09-18\", dto=\"2013-09-18\", wdate=\"2013-09-18\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"a_sep10\", \"sep19_decision\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"b_sep18\", when=\"09/18/2013\", who=\"Party B\", what=\"Bid\", process=\"1\", round=\"3\", type=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Revised final-round indication: a price Party B valued at $21.50 per share, comprising $19.00 cash at closing plus options representing 10% of the new equity (strike equal to Party B's initial cost basis; vesting over five years on achievement of the base-case management projections excluding future acquisitions), which Party B valued at $2.50 of incremental value per share. Bidder-valued package — the option component is non-cash and not guaranteed; All cash = No. Formal as a response to the final-indications solicitation (signal 2). Heavy: financing not committed (09/09) and the Committee later noted the third-party debt financing risk.\",\n formality=\"Formal\", cond=\"Heavy\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with a purchase price that Party B valued at $21.50 per share, including $19.00 of cash to be paid at closing and the remaining per share price to be paid in the form of options to be issued to Mac-Gray stockholders, representing 10% of the new equity with a strike price equal to Party B's initial cost basis.” “These options ... would vest on the achievement of the base case management projections (i.e., over five years), excluding any future acquisitions. Party B's proposal stated that it valued the Party B options at $2.50 of incremental value per share.” (p.36) “Party B would likely be financing the transaction with a combination of equity from affiliated funds and third party debt capital, which would involve more risk than the Pamplona-funded CSC/Pamplona proposal” (P-055, p.37).\",\n source=[\"P-053\", \"P-047\", \"P-055\"], page=36, count=1, review=\"Q5; Q6\",\n plow=21.50, phigh=21.50, pkind=\"Point\", porigin=\"Stated\", currency=\"USD\", allcash=\"No\", cashclose=19.00,\n conddetail=NOTCOMM,\n dfrom=\"2013-09-18\", dto=\"2013-09-18\", wdate=\"2013-09-18\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"b_sep9\", \"sep19_decision\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"c_nosub\", when=\"by 09/18/2013\", who=\"Party C\", what=\"Did not submit\", process=\"1\", round=\"3\", type=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest and did not reiterate its prior $16.00–$17.00 indication in the final-indications solicitation; the filing states it specified no reasons. Stated non-submission; decided by the bidder; no reason given.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest of an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share nor did it specify any reasons in connection therewith.” (p.36) “reported that Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest” (P-054, p.36).\",\n source=[\"P-053\", \"P-054\"], page=36, count=1, review=\"Q4\",\n decidedby=\"Bidder\", exitreason=\"Not stated\", obasis=\"Stated\",\n dfrom=\"\", dto=\"2013-09-18\", wdate=\"2013-09-18\", dbasis=\"Relative only\", dmethod=\"Assigned: deadline\",\n related=[\"c_sep10\", \"dl_sep18\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"sep19_decision\", when=\"09/19/2013\", who=\"Special Committee\", what=\"Target decision\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"3\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"After reviewing the three final proposals and the Projections, the Committee considered CSC/Pamplona the most value with greater certainty and less risk (Party B's package was higher on its face but carried option-measurement risk and third-party debt financing), concluded CSC/Pamplona should be able to raise above $20.75, and authorized the Transaction Committee to inform CSC/Pamplona that the Special Committee was prepared to move into exclusivity at $21.25 per share. Mr. MacDonald indicated he would be supportive of $21.25.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “the Special Committee concluded that the revised indication of interest submitted by CSC/Pamplona had the potential of delivering the most value to stockholders, provided greater certainty and involved less potential risk than the other indications. However, the Special Committee also concluded that, primarily in view of potential synergies between Mac-Gray and CSC, CSC/Pamplona should be in a position to increase their offer price above $20.75. The Special Committee then authorized the Transaction Committee to inform CSC/Pamplona that the Special Committee would be prepared to move into exclusivity at a price of $21.25 per share” “at this meeting Mr. MacDonald indicated that he would be supportive of a price of $21.25 per share” (both p.37).\",\n source=[\"P-054\", \"P-055\"], page=37, review=\"Q1\",\n dfrom=\"2013-09-19\", dto=\"2013-09-19\", wdate=\"2013-09-19\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"csc_sep18\", \"a_reaff\", \"b_sep18\", \"r4_open\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"r4_open\", when=\"09/21/2013\", who=\"Transaction Committee / CSC/Pamplona\",\n what=\"Round opened\", process=\"1\", round=\"4\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Round 4 opened: the Transaction Committee proposed moving forward with CSC/Pamplona exclusively for two weeks subject to an increase to $21.25 per share; CSC/Pamplona confirmed the same day that it would increase its all-cash price to $21.25 as a last and best offer provided Mac-Gray agreed to a two-week exclusive negotiation (exclusivity agreement executed 09/24/2013, R044). Round finality: Inferred final — the target moved to definitive negotiation with the selected bidder; no finality announcement to the other bidders. Round-4 bidder: CSC/Pamplona (1 unit).\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “the members of the Transaction Committee called the representative of CSC/Pamplona to propose that Mac-Gray was prepared to move forward with CSC/Pamplona on an exclusive basis for two weeks subject to CSC/Pamplona increasing their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share. Later that same day, the representative of CSC/Pamplona called the members of the Transaction Committee to confirm that CSC/Pamplona were willing to increase their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share as a last and best offer, provided that Mac-Gray agree to a two week period of exclusive negotiations.” (p.37)\",\n source=[\"P-056\"], page=37, rfinal=\"Inferred final\", review=\"Q1\",\n dfrom=\"2013-09-21\", dto=\"2013-09-21\", wdate=\"2013-09-21\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"sep19_decision\", \"csc_sep21\", \"excl_granted\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"csc_sep21\", when=\"09/21/2013\", who=\"CSC/Pamplona\", what=\"Bid\", process=\"1\", round=\"4\", type=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"All-cash $21.25 per share last and best offer, conditioned on a two-week exclusive negotiation. Part of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal, which also included no financing contingency, Pamplona's commitment to fund 100% of the capital needed for closing, a $15 million reverse termination fee payable if regulatory clearance is not obtained, and post-signing covenants; exclusivity would automatically terminate if CSC/Pamplona adversely changed the proposal terms. Formal: price confirmed as the parties moved to exclusivity and definitive negotiation (signal 3; the same price was carried into the signed merger agreement).\",\n formality=\"Formal\", cond=\"Light\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “CSC/Pamplona were willing to increase their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share as a last and best offer, provided that Mac-Gray agree to a two week period of exclusive negotiations.” (p.37) “the inclusion of a $15 million \"reverse\" termination fee payable by CSC/Pamplona to Mac-Gray in the event regulatory clearance is not obtained” “the fact that there would be no financing contingency and that Pamplona was committing to fund 100% of the capital needed for closing, which, together with the all-cash per share purchase price of $21.25, we refer to as the CSC/Pamplona final proposal” (p.37–38).\",\n source=[\"P-056\", \"P-057\", \"P-059\"], page=37, count=1, review=\"Q5\",\n plow=21.25, phigh=21.25, pkind=\"Point\", porigin=\"Stated\", currency=\"USD\", allcash=\"Yes\", cashclose=21.25,\n conddetail=COMMITTED.format(excl=\"requested (2 wks)\"),\n dfrom=\"2013-09-21\", dto=\"2013-09-21\", wdate=\"2013-09-21\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"csc_sep18\", \"r4_open\", \"excl_auth\", \"signed\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"excl_auth\", when=\"09/23/2013\", who=\"Special Committee\", what=\"Exclusivity changed\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"4\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Exclusivity authorized: the Special Committee authorized Mac-Gray to enter into an exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013 on the terms of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal ($21.25 cash; $15 million CSC reverse termination fee if regulatory clearance not obtained; no financing contingency; Pamplona funding 100% of closing capital; automatic termination on adverse change). This followed negotiation of the agreement's terms 09/21–09/23/2013.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “the Special Committee authorized Mac-Gray to enter into an exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013 on the terms included in the CSC/Pamplona final proposal and authorized the Transaction Committee and Goodwin Procter to continue negotiations with CSC/Pamplona” (p.38). Terms: P-057 (p.37–38).\",\n source=[\"P-057\", \"P-059\"], page=38,\n dfrom=\"2013-09-23\", dto=\"2013-09-23\", wdate=\"2013-09-23\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"csc_sep21\", \"excl_granted\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"excl_granted\", when=\"09/24/2013\", who=\"CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray\", what=\"Exclusivity changed\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"4\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Exclusivity granted: CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013, subject to CSC/Pamplona not adversely changing or modifying the CSC/Pamplona final proposal terms. During exclusivity (09/25–10/07/2013) CSC and Pamplona received full access to the electronic data site and to certain management and conducted confirmatory business and legal diligence.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013, subject to certain conditions, including that CSC and Pamplona not adversely change or modify the terms of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal.” “CSC and Pamplona were granted full access to the electronic data site and access to certain members of management and conducted confirmatory business and legal due diligence on Mac-Gray.” (both p.38)\",\n source=[\"P-060\", \"P-061\"], page=38,\n dfrom=\"2013-09-24\", dto=\"2013-09-24\", wdate=\"2013-09-24\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"excl_auth\", \"a_dropped\", \"b_dropped\", \"excl_ext\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"a_dropped\", when=\"by 09/24/2013\", who=\"Party A\", what=\"Dropped by target\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"4\", type=\"Strategic\",\n terms=\"Inferred: exclusivity — with exclusivity executed with CSC/Pamplona on 09/24/2013, Party A was displaced from the process; no notice to Party A is reported and no earlier outcome is recorded. Count 1.\",\n evidence=\"Inferred: exclusivity. “On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013” (P-060, p.38); Party A was live with its best-and-final offer when CSC/Pamplona was selected (P-053, p.36; P-055, p.37).\",\n source=[\"P-060\", \"P-053\", \"P-055\"], page=38, count=1, review=\"Q4\",\n decidedby=\"Target\", exitreason=\"Not stated\", obasis=\"Inferred: exclusivity\",\n dfrom=\"\", dto=\"2013-09-24\", wdate=\"2013-09-24\", dbasis=\"Relative only\", dmethod=\"Assigned: decision day\",\n related=[\"excl_granted\", \"a_reaff\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"b_dropped\", when=\"by 09/24/2013\", who=\"Party B\", what=\"Dropped by target\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"4\", type=\"Financial\",\n terms=\"Inferred: exclusivity — with exclusivity executed with CSC/Pamplona on 09/24/2013, Party B was displaced from the process; no notice to Party B is reported and no earlier outcome is recorded. Count 1.\",\n evidence=\"Inferred: exclusivity. “On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013” (P-060, p.38); Party B was live with its $21.50-valued package when CSC/Pamplona was selected (P-053, p.36; P-055, p.37).\",\n source=[\"P-060\", \"P-053\", \"P-055\"], page=38, count=1, review=\"Q4\",\n decidedby=\"Target\", exitreason=\"Not stated\", obasis=\"Inferred: exclusivity\",\n dfrom=\"\", dto=\"2013-09-24\", wdate=\"2013-09-24\", dbasis=\"Relative only\", dmethod=\"Assigned: decision day\",\n related=[\"excl_granted\", \"b_sep18\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"kirkland\", when=\"09/25/2013 (earliest observed service; commencement not disclosed)\",\n who=\"Kirkland & Ellis LLP — CSC/Pamplona (client)\", what=\"Adviser service observed\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"4\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona; first observed receiving the initial draft merger agreement from Goodwin Procter on 09/25/2013. Thereafter negotiated the merger agreement, the Pamplona commitment letter (including Pamplona's liability cap) and the voting agreements with Goodwin Procter and counsel for the stockholders through signing. Engagement or selection date not disclosed.\",\n evidence=\"Stated (service; no engagement date). “On September 25, 2013, Goodwin Procter delivered to Kirkland & Ellis LLP, outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona, whom we refer to as Kirkland, the initial draft of the merger agreement.” (p.38) “Kirkland delivered to Goodwin Procter a revised draft of the Pamplona commitment letter which, among other things, proposed that, in addition to CSC, Pamplona would be responsible in the event CSC failed to consummate the merger, but that Pamplona's liability for damages ... would be limited to an unspecified dollar amount.” (p.39)\",\n source=[\"P-061\", \"P-064\"], page=38,\n dfrom=\"2013-09-25\", dto=\"\", wdate=\"2013-09-25\", dbasis=\"Relative only\", dmethod=\"Assigned: bound\",\n related=[\"excl_granted\", \"signed\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"moab_resolved\", when=\"09/23/2013–10/07/2013 (discussions through early October; no rollover determined by 10/07/2013)\",\n who=\"Moab (Mr. Rothenberg) / CSC-Pamplona\", what=\"Material process update\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"4\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Rollover (step 2 — permitted, then resolved without a rollover): Mac-Gray told Mr. Rothenberg on a limited basis of the process status and the CSC/Pamplona negotiations so Moab could resume rollover discussions with CSC/Pamplona; he indicated interest and BofA agreed to arrange and facilitate. Mr. Rothenberg then held discussions with Pamplona; as a result it was determined that Moab would not roll over any shares in the transaction (reported to the Special Committee on 10/07/2013).\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “to provide Moab with the opportunity to resume discussions with CSC/Pamplona regarding a possible equity rollover of Moab's shares in the transaction if Moab still had an interest in such a rollover. Mr. Rothenberg indicated he would like to discuss the possibility of an equity rollover with CSC/Pamplona” (p.38). “Mr. Rothenberg engaged in various discussions with representatives of Pamplona during this time to discuss a possible rollover of Moab shares. As a result of such discussions, it was determined that Moab would not rollover any Moab shares in the transaction.” (p.38) “Mr. Daoust reported to the Special Committee that, after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona, it was determined that Moab would not rollover any Moab shares in the transaction.” (p.39)\",\n source=[\"P-058\", \"P-061\", \"P-065\"], page=39,\n dfrom=\"2013-09-23\", dto=\"2013-10-07\", wdate=\"2013-10-07\", dbasis=\"Reported interval\", dmethod=\"Assigned: decision day\",\n related=[\"moab_denied\", \"moab_proxy\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"excl_ext\", when=\"10/12/2013 (letter agreement; extension sought 10/09–10/11)\",\n who=\"CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray\", what=\"Exclusivity changed\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"4\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Exclusivity extended: with exclusivity due to expire at 5 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013 and open issues remaining, CSC/Pamplona requested an extension; the Special Committee objected to the $15 million Mac-Gray termination fee and would not extend unless a lower amount was agreed; CSC/Pamplona agreed to the $11 million fee, and the parties executed a letter agreement extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on 10/15/2013. Scheduled (not observed) end: the merger agreement was signed 10/14/2013.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “On October 12, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed a letter agreement extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on October 15, 2013.” (p.41) “the Special Committee continued to object to the $15 million Mac-Gray termination fee proposed by CSC/Pamplona and would not be willing to extend exclusivity unless a lower amount were agreed to” “authorized to extend the exclusivity agreement until 11:59 p.m. on ET on October 15, 2013 if CSC/Pamplona would agree to a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million” (p.40) — “Shortly following that conversation, the representative of CSC/Pamplona telephoned Mr. Daoust and agreed to the $11 million Mac-Gray termination fee.” (p.40–41)\",\n source=[\"P-069\", \"P-071\", \"P-072\"], page=41,\n dfrom=\"2013-10-12\", dto=\"2013-10-12\", wdate=\"2013-10-12\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"excl_granted\", \"signed\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"signed\", when=\"10/14/2013\", who=\"Mac-Gray / Special Committee / Board of Directors / CSC-Pamplona\",\n what=\"Merger agreement signed\", process=\"1\", round=\"4\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Agreed consideration: $21.25 per share in cash, without interest and less applicable withholding (whole-company merger; Mac-Gray survives as a wholly-owned subsidiary of Parent). The Special Committee unanimously recommended and the Board unanimously approved and adopted the merger agreement; BofA Merrill Lynch delivered its oral fairness opinion, confirmed in writing dated 10/14/2013. The merger agreement was executed later that day; the Pamplona commitment letter was delivered ($594 million committed by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P.; no financing condition; Pamplona and the Buyer Entities jointly and severally liable for damages, with Pamplona's liability capped at $50 million and the Buyer Entities' liability unlimited); Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement and the MacDonald voting agreements (entered 09/27/2013) became effective — approximately 15% of shares subject to voting agreements. Mac-Gray termination fee $11 million; CSC reverse termination fee $15 million. Signing is not an extra submitted bid: numeric bid-price cells and formality/conditionality cells are blank on this row.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “the Special Committee unanimously determined to recommend to the Board that the merger agreement and the merger were advisable and in the best interests of Mac-Gray's stockholders” (p.41). “the merger agreement was executed, the Pamplona commitment letter was delivered, Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement and the Mac-Donald voting agreements became effective.” (p.41) “Parent will fund the merger consideration from an aggregate of $594 million of capital, ... committed pursuant to a commitment letter delivered to the Buyer Entities by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. dated as of October 14, 2013” (p.6; also Annex A Section 5.08, p. A-30). “Mac-Gray has agreed to pay Parent $11 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances ... Parent has agreed to pay Mac-Gray $15 million ...” (p.10; also p.80–81).\",\n source=[\"P-075\", \"P-076\", \"P-077\", \"X-002\", \"X-005\", \"X-026\", \"X-017\", \"X-018\", \"X-006\"], page=41, review=\"Q5\",\n dfrom=\"2013-10-14\", dto=\"2013-10-14\", wdate=\"2013-10-14\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"csc_sep21\", \"excl_ext\", \"announced\", \"bofa_new\"]),\n\ndict(key=\"announced\", when=\"10/15/2013\", who=\"Mac-Gray and CSC\", what=\"Merger announced\",\n process=\"1\", round=\"4\", type=\"\",\n terms=\"Joint public announcement of the execution of the merger agreement, made before the U.S. stock markets opened. Public disclosure of the transaction; no earlier public sale-process announcement or leak is reported. No go-shop is provided; no post-signing competing proposal is disclosed in the proxy statement.\",\n evidence=\"Stated. “On October 15, 2013, before the U.S. stock markets opened, Mac-Gray and CSC jointly announced the execution of the merger agreement.” (p.41). Absence of a go-shop: the merger agreement prohibits solicitation subject to a fiduciary out — “if, prior to the adoption of the merger agreement by Mac-Gray stockholders, Mac-Gray receives an unsolicited bona fide acquisition proposal in writing ... Mac-Gray may ... enter into, maintain and participate in discussions or negotiations” (p.8); no go-shop provision is described.\",\n source=[\"P-078\", \"X-004\"], page=41,\n dfrom=\"2013-10-15\", dto=\"2013-10-15\", wdate=\"2013-10-15\", dbasis=\"Reported day\", dmethod=\"Reported\",\n related=[\"signed\"]),\n]\n\n# Order of keys defines reading order; sanity check that it matches list order\nKEYS = [r['key'] for r in ROWS]\nassert len(KEYS) == len(set(KEYS)), \"duplicate keys\"\n","path":"/tmp/opencode/ledger_data.py"},"output":"Created file successfully: /tmp/opencode/ledger_data.py","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: /tmp/opencode/ledger_data.py"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Ledger rows for the Mac-Gray / CSC-Pamplona deal (worked from the DEFM14A only).\\n\\nEach row: dict with keys used by build_workbook.py. 'related' references other rows\\nby key, resolved to Row ids at build time.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n# Shorthand for the Conditions detail fixed format\\nNN = \\\"Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: {dd}; Excl: not stated\\\"\\nCOMMITTED = \\\"Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: {excl}\\\"\\nNOTCOMM = \\\"Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated\\\"\\n\\nROWS = [\\ndict(key=\\\"bofa_prior\\\", when=\\\"10/23/2012\\\", who=\\\"BofA Merrill Lynch — Mac-Gray (client)\\\",\\n what=\\\"Adviser engaged\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"0\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Pre-process context (not a Mac-Gray sale attempt): engaged 10/23/2012 for the 2011-2012 Discussions — Mac-Gray's consideration of a possible acquisition of CSC. CSC was itself sold to Pamplona in May 2013. The mandate was terminated in May 2013 before the sale process (see R006).\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “In connection with Mac-Gray's consideration of a possible acquisition of CSC, which we refer to as the 2011-2012 Discussions, Mac-Gray engaged BofA Merrill Lynch on October 23, 2012.” “During the fall and winter of 2012, CSC engaged in a sale process and, ultimately, CSC was purchased by Pamplona in May 2013.” (both p.27)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-002\\\"], page=27,\\n dfrom=\\\"2012-10-23\\\", dto=\\\"2012-10-23\\\", wdate=\\\"2012-10-23\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"bofa_ended\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"apr5\\\", when=\\\"04/05/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray Board of Directors\\\", what=\\\"Target sale decision\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"0\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Board discussed CSC's sale to Pamplona and industry M&A activity and authorized Mac-Gray management to work with BofA Merrill Lynch to explore transactional opportunities, including with Party A (a laundry-industry strategic party); further consideration deferred to the May 9 meeting. An exploration authorization, not a commitment to sell.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “the Board discussed the sale of CSC to Pamplona as well as industry-wide merger and acquisition activity and dynamics, and authorized Mac-Gray management to work with BofA Merrill Lynch to explore transactional opportunities that might be available to Mac-Gray, including opportunities with another strategic party, whom we refer to as Party A, in the laundry facilities management industry.” (p.27)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-003\\\"], page=27,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-04-05\\\", dto=\\\"2013-04-05\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-04-05\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"apr8\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"apr8\\\", when=\\\"04/08/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party A (approached by BofA Merrill Lynch for Mac-Gray)\\\",\\n what=\\\"Contact\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"0\\\", type=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"BofA Merrill Lynch telephoned Party A, as instructed by the Board, to discuss a possible business combination between Party A and Mac-Gray; Party A indicated it might consider one. Direction: Mac-Gray → Party A. First sale-related contact with Party A.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch, as instructed by the Board, telephoned a representative of Party A to discuss generally a possible business combination between Party A and Mac-Gray. During this call, the representative of Party A indicated that Party A might consider a business combination with Mac-Gray.” (p.27)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-004\\\"], page=27, count=1, review=\\\"Q1\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-04-08\\\", dto=\\\"2013-04-08\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-04-08\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"a_jun21\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"may9\\\", when=\\\"05/09/2013–05/10/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray Board of Directors; Transaction Committee\\\",\\n what=\\\"Material process update\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"0\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Board reviewed strategic alternatives with BofA Merrill Lynch and Goodwin Procter and discussed whether to approach third parties about a potential sale; formed the Transaction Committee (Thomas Bullock and Paul Daoust) to recommend and engage a financial advisor and take administrative actions; deferred the sale-process decision to a later meeting. On 05/10/2013 the Transaction Committee decided to invite three nationally recognized investment banks to submit proposals and recommended that, given his significant family stock ownership and a possible equity rollover, Mr. MacDonald not participate in the Board's evaluation of strategic alternatives or negotiations (he could provide perspectives as requested).\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “the Board formed a transaction committee at this meeting, which we refer to as the Transaction Committee, and appointed Thomas Bullock and Paul Daoust, both independent directors, to serve as its members.” “The Transaction Committee was charged with recommending to the Board the selection and engagement of a financial advisor” (both p.28). “determined to invite three nationally recognized investment banks to submit proposals” (p.28). “Mr. MacDonald should not be permitted to participate in the Board's evaluation of strategic alternatives or any negotiations with any interested parties in a sale process” (p.28)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-005\\\", \\\"P-006\\\", \\\"P-007\\\", \\\"P-008\\\"], page=28,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-05-09\\\", dto=\\\"2013-05-10\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-05-09\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported interval\\\", dmethod=\\\"Assigned: midpoint\\\",\\n related=[\\\"bofa_new\\\", \\\"jun12\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"goodwin\\\", when=\\\"05/09/2013 (earliest observed service; commencement not disclosed)\\\",\\n who=\\\"Goodwin Procter LLP — Mac-Gray (client)\\\", what=\\\"Adviser service observed\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"0\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray; first observed advising the Board at the 05/09/2013 Board meeting, then the Transaction Committee and Special Committee through signing (fiduciary reviews, process and agreement negotiation). Engagement or selection date not disclosed in the filing; no adviser row for a later re-engagement.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated (service; no engagement date). “at an in-person meeting of the Board on April 5, 2013, ... representatives from BofA Merrill Lynch and Goodwin Procter LLP, outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray, were also in attendance” — first narrative mention in the background is the May 9, 2013 meeting (p.27–28). The filing does not state an engagement date; service observed from 05/09/2013.\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-005\\\"], page=28,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-05-09\\\", dto=\\\"\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-05-09\\\", dbasis=\\\"Relative only\\\", dmethod=\\\"Assigned: bound\\\",\\n related=[\\\"bofa_new\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"bofa_ended\\\", when=\\\"05/14/2013–05/15/2013 (committee decision 05/14; letter sent 05/15)\\\",\\n who=\\\"Transaction Committee / BofA Merrill Lynch\\\", what=\\\"Adviser ended\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"0\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Transaction Committee determined to terminate BofA Merrill Lynch's engagement letter entered for the 2011-2012 Discussions; Mac-Gray sent the termination letter 05/15/2013. Reason disclosed: BofA was one of the banks invited to submit a proposal for the new mandate and the CSC sale process had ended.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “Given that BofA Merrill Lynch was one of the investment banks to be invited to submit a proposal and that the CSC sale process had ended, the Transaction Committee determined to terminate BofA Merrill Lynch's engagement letter entered into for purposes of the 2011-2012 Discussions.” “On May 15, 2013, Mac-Gray sent a letter to BofA Merrill Lynch terminating their engagement in connection with the 2011-2012 Discussions.” (both p.29)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-009\\\", \\\"P-010\\\"], page=29,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-05-14\\\", dto=\\\"2013-05-15\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-05-14\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported interval\\\", dmethod=\\\"Assigned: bound\\\",\\n related=[\\\"bofa_prior\\\", \\\"bofa_new\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"bofa_new\\\", when=\\\"05/30/2013–05/31/2013 (Board approval 05/30; engagement letter 05/31)\\\",\\n who=\\\"BofA Merrill Lynch — Mac-Gray (client)\\\", what=\\\"Adviser engaged\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"0\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Board unanimously approved engaging BofA Merrill Lynch as Mac-Gray's financial advisor for the strategic-alternatives review and potential sale process; BofA had presented 05/22/2013, the other two invited candidates 05/29/2013. Engagement letter entered 05/31/2013; BofA agreed not to act as a source of new acquisition financing for potential buyers without Mac-Gray's prior written consent. BofA advised through signing and delivered its written fairness opinion dated 10/14/2013; its fee includes a portion payable on the opinion and a significant portion contingent on consummation.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “Based on the recommendation of the Transaction Committee, the Board unanimously approved the engagement of BofA Merrill Lynch on the terms discussed at this meeting.” (p.29) “On May 31, 2013, Mac-Gray entered into an engagement letter with BofA Merrill Lynch with respect to the Board's undertaking a review of strategic alternatives, including a potential sale process, and in which BofA Merrill Lynch agreed not to engage as a possible source of new acquisition financing for any potential buyers in connection with any such sale process without Mac-Gray's prior written consent.” (p.30) “We have acted as financial advisor to MGC in connection with the Merger and will receive a fee for our services, a portion of which is payable upon the rendering of this opinion and a significant portion of which is contingent upon consummation of the Merger.” (Annex B, p. B-2)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-011\\\", \\\"P-012\\\", \\\"P-013\\\", \\\"P-014\\\", \\\"P-016\\\", \\\"X-028\\\"], page=30,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-05-30\\\", dto=\\\"2013-05-31\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-05-30\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported interval\\\", dmethod=\\\"Assigned: bound\\\",\\n related=[\\\"bofa_ended\\\", \\\"signed\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"moab_proxy\\\", when=\\\"05/30/2013\\\", who=\\\"Moab / Mac-Gray annual stockholder meeting\\\",\\n what=\\\"Activist involvement\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"0\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Moab-nominated candidates Michael M. Rothenberg (Moab co-founder and General Partner) and James E. Hyman were elected as directors in place of two incumbent nominees after a proxy contest; board size was reduced to seven. Context: the board change led to Mr. Rothenberg's exclusion from the sale process given Moab's possible equity rollover interest; Moab held approximately 9% (06/12/2013).\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “Mac-Gray and Moab engaged in a proxy contest leading up to the annual meeting and Mr. Rothenberg and Mr. Hyman were elected in place of Mac-Gray's incumbent nominees, David W. Bryan and Mary Ann Tocio.” “Mr. Rothenberg is a co-founder and the General Partner of Moab” (both p.29). “At the time of this meeting, Moab beneficially owned approximately 9% of Mac-Gray's outstanding common stock.” (p.30)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-015\\\", \\\"P-017\\\"], page=29,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-05-30\\\", dto=\\\"2013-05-30\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-05-30\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"jun12\\\", \\\"moab_denied\\\", \\\"moab_resolved\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"jun12\\\", when=\\\"06/12/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray / new directors (Rothenberg, Hyman)\\\",\\n what=\\\"Material process update\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"0\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Orientation of new directors: each received an overview of the strategic-alternatives review and potential sale process; with Mr. Rothenberg the participants discussed that if Moab might want an equity rollover in a sale transaction resulting from the process, he would need to be excluded from the process from the outset. Moab then held approximately 9% of Mac-Gray's outstanding stock.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “to the extent Moab might have an interest in an equity rollover of all or a portion of Moab's shares of Mac-Gray common stock in connection with any sale transaction that might result from the Board's strategic alternatives process, Mr. Rothenberg would need to be excluded from the process from the outset. At the time of this meeting, Moab beneficially owned approximately 9% of Mac-Gray's outstanding common stock.” (p.30)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-017\\\"], page=30,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-06-12\\\", dto=\\\"2013-06-12\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-06-12\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"moab_proxy\\\", \\\"r1_open\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"a_jun21\\\", when=\\\"06/21/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party A\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"0\\\", type=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Unsolicited proposal to the Board for a whole-company acquisition at an all-cash price of $17.00–$19.00 per share. Made before any substantive diligence access (no confidentiality agreement yet; Party A's NDA was executed 08/05/2013), so Heavy by context. Still standing when round 1 was evaluated (reviewed with the three preliminary indications at the 07/25/2013 Special Committee meeting).\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated (price). “On June 21, 2013, Party A submitted an unsolicited proposal to the Mac-Gray Board of Directors offering to purchase Mac-Gray for an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $19.00 per share” (p.30). Context: no substantive access before the proposal — “outside counsel to Party A and representatives of Goodwin Procter negotiated the terms of a confidentiality and standstill agreement, but did not come to agreement on the terms of the customer and employee non-solicitation provisions” between 07/11 and 07/23 (P-030, p.33); reviewed as still standing on 07/25/2013 (P-033, p.33).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-018\\\", \\\"P-030\\\", \\\"P-033\\\"], page=30, count=1, review=\\\"Q1; Q5\\\",\\n plow=17.00, phigh=19.00, pkind=\\\"Bidder range\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", currency=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=\\\"\\\",\\n conddetail=NN.format(dd=\\\"no\\\"),\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-06-21\\\", dto=\\\"2013-06-21\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-06-21\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"apr8\\\", \\\"r1_open\\\", \\\"a_sep10\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"r1_open\\\", when=\\\"06/24/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray Board of Directors / Special Committee\\\",\\n what=\\\"Round opened\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"1\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"R1 anchor: 06/24/2013 Special Committee determination to commence the sale process and approach 50 parties (15 strategic, 35 financial) — first outreach executed within days (contacts reported 06/28/2013). Rejected anchor candidates: R003 (04/08/2013 single Party A contact) and R009 (06/21/2013 unsolicited Party A proposal). The Board also excluded Mr. MacDonald and Mr. Rothenberg from evaluating strategic alternatives (possible rollovers) and established the Special Committee (Bullock chair; Daoust, Hyman, Meagher, Percelay, Robinson). Deadline set: preliminary indications of interest due 07/23/2013 (informational package issued to NDA signers). Round finality: Not final — initial solicitation for preliminary indications; no finality signal.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “the Special Committee concluded that it would be in the best interests of stockholders to consider a potential sale of Mac-Gray” (p.31). “the Board decided, and Mr. MacDonald and Mr. Rothenberg agreed, that it would be appropriate to exclude Mr. MacDonald and Mr. Rothenberg from the Board's evaluation of strategic alternatives and any negotiations with third parties that might take place” (p.30). “a total of 50 parties, including CSC and Pamplona, who together we refer to as CSC/Pamplona, and Party A, to solicit potential interest in a transaction with Mac-Gray, 15 of which were potential strategic buyers and 35 of which were potential financial buyers, including private equity firms” (p.32). “furnished an informational package for the purpose of providing potential bidders with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest, which they were instructed to submit by July 23, 2013” (p.32)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-019\\\", \\\"P-021\\\", \\\"P-022\\\", \\\"P-023\\\"], page=31, due=\\\"2013-07-23\\\", rfinal=\\\"Not final\\\", review=\\\"Q1\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-06-24\\\", dto=\\\"2013-06-24\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-06-24\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"a_jun21\\\", \\\"apr8\\\", \\\"contact_strat\\\", \\\"dl_jul23\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"contact_strat\\\", when=\\\"late June 2013 (after the 06/24/2013 decision; contacts reported by 06/28/2013)\\\",\\n who=\\\"BofA Merrill Lynch (for Mac-Gray) — strategic parties\\\", what=\\\"Contact\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"1\\\", type=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Outreach wave to the 15 potential strategic buyers identified at the 06/24/2013 meeting, including Party A and CSC/Pamplona; Party A was already in contact from 04/08/2013. Part of the 50-party universe; 2 of the 15 (Party A, CSC/Pamplona) ultimately executed confidentiality agreements.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “BofA Merrill Lynch contacted the strategic and financial parties identified at the June 24th Special Committee meeting” (p.32); “a total of 50 parties, ... 15 of which were potential strategic buyers and 35 of which were potential financial buyers” (p.32); “including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona)” signed confidentiality agreements (p.32).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-022\\\", \\\"P-023\\\"], page=32, count=15,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-06-24\\\", dto=\\\"\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-06-24\\\", dbasis=\\\"Relative only\\\", dmethod=\\\"Assigned: bound\\\",\\n related=[\\\"r1_open\\\", \\\"apr8\\\", \\\"contact_fin\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"contact_fin\\\", when=\\\"late June 2013 (after the 06/24/2013 decision; contacts reported by 06/28/2013)\\\",\\n who=\\\"BofA Merrill Lynch (for Mac-Gray) — financial parties\\\", what=\\\"Contact\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"1\\\", type=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Outreach wave to the 35 potential financial buyers identified at the 06/24/2013 meeting, including private equity firms (among them Party B and Party C); 18 of the 35 ultimately executed confidentiality agreements (including Party B and Party C).\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “BofA Merrill Lynch contacted the strategic and financial parties identified at the June 24th Special Committee meeting” (p.32); “35 of which were potential financial buyers, including private equity firms”; “18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C)” signed confidentiality agreements (p.32).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-022\\\", \\\"P-023\\\"], page=32, count=35,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-06-24\\\", dto=\\\"\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-06-24\\\", dbasis=\\\"Relative only\\\", dmethod=\\\"Assigned: bound\\\",\\n related=[\\\"r1_open\\\", \\\"contact_strat\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"resid_nda\\\", when=\\\"late June–August 2013 (two-month signing window; dates not individually disclosed)\\\",\\n who=\\\"16 residual financial NDA signers\\\", what=\\\"NDA signed\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"1\\\", type=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Residual cohort: 18 financial NDA signers less the two individually recorded financial signers (Party B, Party C) = 16 financial NDA signers. The filing reports the 20 signers collectively over a two-month window and does not date them; the two strategic signers (Party A, CSC/Pamplona) are recorded individually. Agreements were on a form provided by Mac-Gray, individually negotiated but not materially varied; they included standstill provisions with sunset rights to make confidential proposals on announcement of a business combination. Working date is the first day of the reported signing window (display convention) — not an observed signing date. Count 16.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated (population and window). “Over the next two months a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C), entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray on a form provided by Mac-Gray, the terms of which were individually negotiated with potential bidders, but did not vary materially from the form provided.” “The confidentiality agreements contained customary non-disclosure provisions and a customary standstill provision that either expired or permitted the potential bidder to make confidential proposals to Mac-Gray (a so-called \\\"sunset\\\" provision) upon announcement of a business combination between Mac-Gray and a third party” (both p.32).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-023\\\"], page=32, count=16, review=\\\"Q3; Q7\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-06-24\\\", dto=\\\"2013-08-31\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-06-24\\\", dbasis=\\\"Approximate window\\\", dmethod=\\\"Assigned: bound\\\",\\n related=[\\\"resid_nosub\\\", \\\"b_nda\\\", \\\"c_nda\\\", \\\"csc_nda\\\", \\\"a_nda\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"b_nda\\\", when=\\\"06/28/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party B\\\", what=\\\"NDA signed\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"1\\\", type=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Party B entered a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided the informational package (preliminary indication of interest due 07/23/2013). First observed participation by Party B.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “Later on June 28, 2013, Party B, entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package for the purpose of providing Party B with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest.” (p.32)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-025\\\"], page=32, count=1, review=\\\"Q3\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-06-28\\\", dto=\\\"2013-06-28\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-06-28\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"b_jul24\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"c_nda\\\", when=\\\"06/30/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party C\\\", what=\\\"NDA signed\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"1\\\", type=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Party C entered a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided the informational package (preliminary indication of interest due 07/23/2013). First observed participation by Party C.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “On June 30, 2013, Party C entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package for the purpose of providing Party C with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest.” (p.32)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-026\\\"], page=32, count=1, review=\\\"Q3\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-06-30\\\", dto=\\\"2013-06-30\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-06-30\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"c_jul24\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"moab_denied\\\", when=\\\"07/06/2013\\\", who=\\\"Special Committee / Moab / CSC/Pamplona\\\",\\n what=\\\"Material process update\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"1\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Rollover (step 1 — exclusivity denied): the Special Committee denied the request that Moab be permitted to partner exclusively with CSC/Pamplona (including sharing under CSC/Pamplona's confidentiality agreement), so that Moab's potential equity rollover remained available as a source of capital for other bidders; the Committee told the parties it was premature and that rollover discussions would be permitted at a later stage. Mr. Rothenberg had raised Moab's interest with Goodwin Procter on 07/03/2013.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “the Special Committee decided to deny the exclusivity request at this stage of the process so that the potential equity rollover of Moab's shares could be available as a source of capital for other potential bidders. The Special Committee instructed BofA Merrill Lynch and Goodwin Procter to communicate to CSC/Pamplona and Mr. Rothenberg, respectively, that it was premature for Mac-Gray to permit Moab to engage in equity rollover discussions with any party, including CSC/Pamplona, but that such discussions would be permitted at a later stage of the sale process.” (p.32–33)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-027\\\", \\\"P-028\\\"], page=32,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-07-06\\\", dto=\\\"2013-07-06\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-07-06\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"moab_proxy\\\", \\\"moab_resolved\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"csc_nda\\\", when=\\\"07/11/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC/Pamplona\\\", what=\\\"NDA signed\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"1\\\", type=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"CSC/Pamplona entered a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided the informational package. The merger agreement later confirms the July 11, 2013 confidentiality letter agreement among Pamplona Capital Management LLC, Parent and Mac-Gray.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “On July 11, 2013, CSC/Pamplona entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and were provided with an informational package for the purpose of providing CSC/Pamplona with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest.” (p.33) “Parent and the Company hereby acknowledge and agree that they are and shall continue to be bound by that certain letter agreement dated as of July 11, 2013, among Pamplona Capital Management LLC, Parent and the Company (the \\\"Confidentiality Agreement\\\").” (Annex A, Section 6.17, p. A-46)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-029\\\", \\\"X-027\\\"], page=33, count=1, review=\\\"Q3\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-07-11\\\", dto=\\\"2013-07-11\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-07-11\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"csc_jul23\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"dl_jul23\\\", when=\\\"07/23/2013 (scheduled due date for preliminary indications)\\\",\\n who=\\\"NDA signers (solicitation deadline)\\\", what=\\\"Deadline\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"1\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Preliminary indications of interest were due 07/23/2013 (deadline set with the launch of the process; see R010). CSC/Pamplona submitted on the due date; Party B (07/24) and Party C (07/24–25) submitted after it and were considered (late bids accepted). No extension is disclosed.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated (due date reached and operative). “furnished an informational package for the purpose of providing potential bidders with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest, which they were instructed to submit by July 23, 2013” (p.32); submissions and later consideration documented at P-031, P-032, P-033, P-035.\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-023\\\", \\\"P-031\\\", \\\"P-032\\\", \\\"P-033\\\", \\\"P-035\\\"], page=32, due=\\\"2013-07-23\\\",\\n dltreatment=\\\"Late bids accepted\\\", review=\\\"Q2\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-07-23\\\", dto=\\\"2013-07-23\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-07-23\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"r1_open\\\", \\\"csc_jul23\\\", \\\"resid_nosub\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"csc_jul23\\\", when=\\\"07/23/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC/Pamplona\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"1\\\", type=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Preliminary indication of interest, all-cash $18.50 per share, submitted on the 07/23/2013 deadline. First bid by CSC/Pamplona (NDA 07/11/2013; preliminary review only — no substantive data-site or management access yet, so Heavy by context).\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “On July 23, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share.” (p.33) Context: “Between July 11, 2013 and July 23, 2013, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona engaged in a preliminary review of Mac-Gray and the potential acquisition opportunity.” (p.33); management presentations and data-site access came later (P-042, p.34).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-031\\\", \\\"P-030\\\", \\\"P-042\\\"], page=33, count=1, review=\\\"Q5\\\",\\n plow=18.50, phigh=18.50, pkind=\\\"Point\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", currency=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=18.50,\\n conddetail=NN.format(dd=\\\"yes\\\"),\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-07-23\\\", dto=\\\"2013-07-23\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-07-23\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"csc_nda\\\", \\\"csc_sep9\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"resid_nosub\\\", when=\\\"by 07/23/2013\\\", who=\\\"16 residual financial NDA signers\\\", what=\\\"Did not submit\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"1\\\", type=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Inferred: residual — 20 NDA signers (2 strategic + 18 financial) − 4 individually recorded participants (Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona) = 16 residual financial signers with no preliminary indication of interest submitted by the 07/23/2013 deadline; the filing names no other submitters, and the 07/25/2013 Special Committee review addressed only Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona and the standing Party A proposal. Base assumes the residual signers had signed by and were eligible for the solicitation; the filing dates their signatures only as a two-month window. No motive, identity or voluntary withdrawal inferred.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Inferred: residual. “a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C), entered into confidentiality agreements” (P-023, p.32); “representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch reviewed the preliminary indications of interest received from Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona as well as the Party A June 21 proposal” (P-033, p.33). Arithmetic: 20 − 4 = 16.\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-023\\\", \\\"P-033\\\"], page=33, count=16, review=\\\"Q3; Q4\\\",\\n decidedby=\\\"Unknown\\\", exitreason=\\\"Not stated\\\", obasis=\\\"Inferred: residual\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"\\\", dto=\\\"2013-07-23\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-07-23\\\", dbasis=\\\"Relative only\\\", dmethod=\\\"Assigned: deadline\\\",\\n related=[\\\"resid_nda\\\", \\\"dl_jul23\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"b_jul24\\\", when=\\\"07/24/2013 (one day after the 07/23/2013 due date)\\\", who=\\\"Party B\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"1\\\", type=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Preliminary indication of interest, all-cash $17.00–$18.00 per share, submitted after the 07/23/2013 due date and considered at the 07/25/2013 Special Committee meeting (late bid accepted). Preliminary review only; Heavy by context.\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “On July 24, 2013, Party B submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $18.00 per share.” (p.33) Considered: “reviewed the preliminary indications of interest received from Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona” (p.33).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-032\\\", \\\"P-033\\\"], page=33, count=1, review=\\\"Q2; Q5\\\",\\n plow=17.00, phigh=18.00, pkind=\\\"Bidder range\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", currency=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=\\\"\\\",\\n conddetail=NN.format(dd=\\\"yes\\\"),\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-07-24\\\", dto=\\\"2013-07-24\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-07-24\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"b_nda\\\", \\\"b_sep9\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"c_jul24\\\", when=\\\"07/24/2013–07/25/2013 (oral indication 07/24; written indication 07/25)\\\",\\n who=\\\"Party C\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"1\\\", type=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Oral preliminary indication of interest 07/24/2013 at $15.00–$17.00 per share, followed by a written indication of interest 07/25/2013 at $16.00–$16.50 per share; treated as one bid (an IOI and its written offer are one submission). The written indication came after the 07/23/2013 due date and was considered (late bid accepted). Preliminary review only; Heavy by context.\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “representatives from Party C called BofA Merrill Lynch and presented an oral preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $15.00 to $17.00 per share” (p.33). “Later on July 25, 2013, Party C submitted a written indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $16.50 per share.” (p.34) Considered at the 07/25/2013 Special Committee meeting (P-033, p.33).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-032\\\", \\\"P-033\\\", \\\"P-035\\\"], page=34, count=1, review=\\\"Q2; Q5; Q7\\\",\\n plow=16.00, phigh=16.50, pkind=\\\"Bidder range\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", currency=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=\\\"\\\",\\n conddetail=NN.format(dd=\\\"yes\\\"),\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-07-24\\\", dto=\\\"2013-07-25\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-07-24\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported interval\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"c_nda\\\", \\\"c_sep10\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"r2_open\\\", when=\\\"07/25/2013\\\", who=\\\"Special Committee\\\", what=\\\"Round opened\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"2\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Round 2 opened: Special Committee reviewed the three preliminary indications (Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona) and the still-standing Party A June 21 proposal; indications were lower than expected; adopted staged disclosure of sensitive information for the second stage. Authorized BofA to arrange management presentations and high-level information access with the four interested bidders (Party A conditional on executing its NDA; synergies discussions for Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and thereafter to request revised indications. Mr. Rothenberg to recuse himself for the duration of the process (continuing rollover interest). Round finality: Not final — revised written proposals were sought only to continue in the process; no finality signal. Round-2 bidders: Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona (4 units).\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “the Special Committee concluded that it would be advisable to stage the disclosure of such information to each of the bidders to the extent that a bidder's indication of interest and other actions demonstrated its seriousness in acquiring Mac-Gray on terms viewed favorably by the Special Committee.” “the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure as discussed at this meeting and to reach out to each of the four interested bidders and arrange management meetings” (both p.33–34). “decided that Mr. Rothenberg should be asked to recuse himself from participating in Board meetings for the duration of the sale process” (p.33).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-033\\\", \\\"P-034\\\"], page=34, rfinal=\\\"Not final\\\", review=\\\"Q1\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-07-25\\\", dto=\\\"2013-07-25\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-07-25\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"r1_open\\\", \\\"a_nda\\\", \\\"info_access\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"a_nda\\\", when=\\\"08/05/2013 (negotiations from 07/11–07/23; resumed 07/27)\\\", who=\\\"Party A\\\",\\n what=\\\"NDA signed\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"2\\\", type=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Party A entered a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and received the informational package to potentially improve its June 21 proposal. Non-solicitation terms were agreed with the Transaction Committee on 07/27/2013 (the filing prints “July 27, 2103” — a typo retained; the supported reading is 07/27/2013). Party A's standing round-0 proposal remained under consideration.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “Discussions with Party A resumed on July 27, 2103 and Party A and the Transaction Committee agreed to the terms of the customer and employee non-solicitation provisions. On August 5, 2013, Party A entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package for the purpose of providing Party A with data to potentially improve the terms of the Party A June 21 proposal.” (p.34) Wording of the source typo preserved; proposed corrected date 07/27/2013 (see Q7).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-030\\\", \\\"P-036\\\"], page=34, count=1, review=\\\"Q3; Q7\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-08-05\\\", dto=\\\"2013-08-05\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-08-05\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"a_jun21\\\", \\\"info_access\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"info_access\\\", when=\\\"08/06/2013–08/27/2013 (staged access during diligence)\\\",\\n who=\\\"Mac-Gray/BofA Merrill Lynch → Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona\\\",\\n what=\\\"Information access changed\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"2\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Differentiated, staged access among the four live bidders: Party B and Party C (financial bidders) received broad access to the electronic data site; Party A and CSC/Pamplona (strategic bidders) received somewhat limited access, with customer data (including locations) reserved until later in the process. Stated rationale: risk of misuse of sensitive competitive information by strategic bidders (07/25/2013 staging decision). Management presentations were held for each advanced bidder (B 08/06; C 08/08; CSC/Pamplona 08/12; A 08/14); Party A and CSC/Pamplona also held synergies discussions with management.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “Party B and Party C, in light of the fact that they were financial bidders, were given broad access to an electronic data site, and Party A and CSC/Pamplona, in light of the fact that they were strategic bidders, were given somewhat limited access to this electronic data site, with access to customer data, including customer locations, being reserved until later in the process as part of the staging discussed at the July 25th Special Committee meeting.” “both Party A and CSC/Pamplona participated in discussions with members of Mac-Gray management around synergies.” (both p.34) Presentations at P-037–P-040 (p.34).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-033\\\", \\\"P-034\\\", \\\"P-037\\\", \\\"P-038\\\", \\\"P-039\\\", \\\"P-040\\\", \\\"P-041\\\", \\\"P-042\\\"], page=34,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-08-06\\\", dto=\\\"2013-08-27\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-08-06\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported interval\\\", dmethod=\\\"Assigned: bound\\\",\\n related=[\\\"r2_open\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"dlset_sep9\\\", when=\\\"08/27/2013\\\", who=\\\"BofA Merrill Lynch (for the Special Committee)\\\",\\n what=\\\"Deadline set\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"2\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Following the 08/15/2013 Special Committee authorization, BofA sent a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona requesting revised written proposals no later than 09/09/2013 to continue in the process and pursue in-depth confirmatory diligence; the letter asked for valuation, financing sources/structure, regulatory approvals, post-signing covenants and diligence focus areas.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “BofA Merrill Lynch, as instructed by the Special Committee, sent a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013 if such bidders wished to proceed further in the process to pursue an in-depth evaluation of Mac-Gray with the objective of making a revised offer.” (p.35) Authorization: “the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to send a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona once all four of the bidders' due diligence was substantially complete requesting that ... such party submit a revised written proposal in order to continue in the process” (p.34).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-041\\\", \\\"P-043\\\"], page=35, due=\\\"2013-09-09\\\", review=\\\"Q2\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-08-27\\\", dto=\\\"2013-08-27\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-08-27\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"dl_sep9\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"dl_sep9\\\", when=\\\"09/09/2013 (scheduled due date for revised written proposals)\\\",\\n who=\\\"Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona (solicitation deadline)\\\", what=\\\"Deadline\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"2\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Revised written proposals were due 09/09/2013. CSC/Pamplona and Party B submitted on the due date; Party A and Party C submitted on 09/10/2013 and were considered at the 09/11/2013 Special Committee meeting (late bids accepted; no extension disclosed).\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated (due date reached and operative). “instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013” (p.35); submissions at P-047 and P-048; considered: “the Special Committee held a telephonic meeting to review the revised indications of interest submitted by Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona” on 09/11/2013 (P-050, p.35).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-043\\\", \\\"P-047\\\", \\\"P-048\\\", \\\"P-050\\\"], page=35, due=\\\"2013-09-09\\\",\\n dltreatment=\\\"Late bids accepted\\\", review=\\\"Q2\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-09\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-09\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-09\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"dlset_sep9\\\", \\\"csc_sep9\\\", \\\"b_sep9\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"csc_sep9\\\", when=\\\"09/09/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC/Pamplona\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"2\\\", type=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Revised indication of interest: all-cash $19.50 per share; Pamplona committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction; requested two weeks of exclusive negotiations. Light: committed financing, no diligence condition reported (exclusivity request does not change the level).\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Light\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “On September 9, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $19.50 per share, indicating that Pamplona was committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction and requesting that CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray agree to exclusive negotiations for two weeks.” (p.35)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-047\\\"], page=35, count=1, review=\\\"Q5\\\",\\n plow=19.50, phigh=19.50, pkind=\\\"Point\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", currency=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=19.50,\\n conddetail=COMMITTED.format(excl=\\\"requested (2 wks)\\\"),\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-09\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-09\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-09\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"csc_jul23\\\", \\\"csc_sep18\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"b_sep9\\\", when=\\\"09/09/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party B\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"2\\\", type=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Revised indication of interest: all-cash $18.50 per share; proposed financing from a combination of affiliated-fund equity and third-party debt; no firm financing commitment (stated) — Heavy.\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share and proposed to finance the transaction with a combination of equity from affiliated funds and third party debt. Party B's revised indication of interest did not include a firm financing commitment.” (p.35)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-047\\\"], page=35, count=1, review=\\\"Q5\\\",\\n plow=18.50, phigh=18.50, pkind=\\\"Point\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", currency=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=18.50,\\n conddetail=NOTCOMM,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-09\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-09\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-09\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"b_jul24\\\", \\\"b_sep18\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"a_sep10\\\", when=\\\"09/10/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party A\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"2\\\", type=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Revised indication of interest: all-cash $18.00–$19.00 per share, to be financed by outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity sources; no firm financing commitment (stated) — Heavy.\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “On September 10, 2013, Party A submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share, to be financed by outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity sources.” “Neither Party A's nor Party C's revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment.” (both p.35)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-048\\\"], page=35, count=1, review=\\\"Q5\\\",\\n plow=18.00, phigh=19.00, pkind=\\\"Bidder range\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", currency=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=\\\"\\\",\\n conddetail=NOTCOMM,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-10\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-10\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-10\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"a_jun21\\\", \\\"a_reaff\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"c_sep10\\\", when=\\\"09/10/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party C\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"2\\\", type=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Revised oral indication of interest (telephone call to BofA Merrill Lynch): all-cash $16.00–$17.00 per share; no firm financing commitment (stated) — Heavy.\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Informal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch, a representative of Party C indicated that it was submitting a revised oral indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share. Neither Party A's nor Party C's revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment.” (p.35)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-048\\\"], page=35, count=1, review=\\\"Q5\\\",\\n plow=16.00, phigh=17.00, pkind=\\\"Bidder range\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", currency=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=\\\"\\\",\\n conddetail=NOTCOMM,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-10\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-10\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-10\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"c_jul24\\\", \\\"c_nosub\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"macd_decline\\\", when=\\\"09/11/2013\\\", who=\\\"Transaction Committee → Mr. MacDonald (rollover)\\\",\\n what=\\\"Material process update\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"2\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Rollover (declined): the Transaction Committee gave Mr. MacDonald, without identifying bidders or prices, a limited overview of the process status so he could consider whether he remained interested in a possible rollover of his Mac-Gray shares; he stated he had decided he was not interested in rolling over any shares in any transaction.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “provided Mr. MacDonald with a limited overview of the status of the Special Committee's review of strategic alternatives ... so that Mr. MacDonald could consider whether he continued to have an interest in potentially rolling over any of his Mac-Gray shares in a transaction. During this call, Mr. MacDonald indicated that he had decided that he was not interested in rolling over any of his shares in any transaction.” (p.35)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-049\\\"], page=35,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-11\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-11\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-11\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"r3_open\\\", \\\"macd_brief\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"r3_open\\\", when=\\\"09/11/2013\\\", who=\\\"Special Committee\\\", what=\\\"Round opened\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"3\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Round 3 opened: after BofA reported it was unlikely any bidder would proceed without Mr. MacDonald's express support and the Committee agreed his perspective on price was critical, the Special Committee instructed BofA to call Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona to request final indications of interest by 09/18/2013 and to indicate that Mac-Gray would consider a short period of exclusive negotiations with one bidder depending on price and deal certainty. Deadline set: final indications due 09/18/2013. Round finality: Announced as final — bidders were told this was the final indications stage. Round-3 bidders: Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona (4 invited).\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “the Special Committee instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to call each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013 and to indicate that Mac-Gray would consider engaging in a short period of exclusive negotiations with one of the bidders depending upon, among other things, the proposed purchase price and the level of deal certainty indicated in the bidder's final proposal.” “any potential acquiror would be unlikely to proceed without knowing that Mr. MacDonald would support the transaction.” (both p.36)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-050\\\"], page=36, due=\\\"2013-09-18\\\", rfinal=\\\"Announced as final\\\", review=\\\"Q1\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-11\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-11\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-11\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"macd_decline\\\", \\\"macd_brief\\\", \\\"dl_sep18\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"macd_brief\\\", when=\\\"09/12/2013\\\", who=\\\"BofA Merrill Lynch → Mr. MacDonald\\\",\\n what=\\\"Material process update\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"3\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Mr. MacDonald received a detailed overview of the process, the status of negotiations and the identities of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona; he voiced general support for continuing the process but expressed the view that Mac-Gray should continue to seek a higher value for stockholders.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch participated in a telephone conference call with Mr. MacDonald and provided him with a detailed overview of the strategic alternatives process, including the status of negotiations with and the identity of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona. Although Mr. MacDonald voiced his general support for continuing with the process, he expressed his view that Mac-Gray should continue to seek a higher value for stockholders.” (p.36)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-051\\\"], page=36,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-12\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-12\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-12\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"r3_open\\\", \\\"sep19_decision\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"dl_sep18\\\", when=\\\"09/18/2013 (scheduled due date for final indications)\\\",\\n who=\\\"Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona (solicitation deadline)\\\", what=\\\"Deadline\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"3\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Final indications of interest were due 09/18/2013. CSC/Pamplona and Party B submitted, Party A reiterated its prior offer, and Party C did not submit. The Special Committee evaluated the proposals on 09/19/2013 (enforced: the date passed with no extension and the target took its next step on the bids in hand).\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated (due date reached and operative). “request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013” (p.36); submissions and evaluation at P-053 and P-054. No extension disclosed; selection followed 09/19/2013 (P-055, p.37).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-050\\\", \\\"P-053\\\", \\\"P-054\\\", \\\"P-055\\\"], page=36, due=\\\"2013-09-18\\\",\\n dltreatment=\\\"Enforced\\\", review=\\\"Q2\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-18\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-18\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-18\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"r3_open\\\", \\\"csc_sep18\\\", \\\"c_nosub\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"csc_sep18\\\", when=\\\"09/18/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC/Pamplona\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"3\\\", type=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Final-round proposal: all-cash $20.75 per share; Pamplona committed to provide 100% of the capital required; requested two weeks of exclusive negotiations. Formal as a response on the requested basis to the target's final-indications solicitation (signal 2). Light: committed financing and no diligence condition reported.\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Formal\\\", cond=\\\"Light\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “On September 18, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share, reiterating that Pamplona was committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction and requesting that CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray agree to engage in exclusive negotiations for two weeks.” (p.36) Final solicitation: “request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013” (P-050, p.36).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-053\\\", \\\"P-050\\\"], page=36, count=1, review=\\\"Q5\\\",\\n plow=20.75, phigh=20.75, pkind=\\\"Point\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", currency=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=20.75,\\n conddetail=COMMITTED.format(excl=\\\"requested (2 wks)\\\"),\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-18\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-18\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-18\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"csc_sep9\\\", \\\"sep19_decision\\\", \\\"csc_sep21\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"a_reaff\\\", when=\\\"09/18/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party A\\\", what=\\\"Bid reaffirmed\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"3\\\", type=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Party A reiterated by telephone that its previous $18.00–$19.00 all-cash indication was its best and final offer; no new price. Formal as a supported best-and-final response to the target's final-indications solicitation (signal 2). Heavy: no firm financing commitment was ever reported.\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Formal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated (reaffirmation). “Party A reiterated in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer.” (p.36) Financing position carried: “Neither Party A's nor Party C's revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment.” (P-048, p.35)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-053\\\", \\\"P-048\\\"], page=36, count=1, review=\\\"Q5\\\",\\n plow=18.00, phigh=19.00, pkind=\\\"Bidder range\\\", porigin=\\\"Carried forward\\\", currency=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=\\\"\\\",\\n conddetail=NOTCOMM,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-18\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-18\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-18\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"a_sep10\\\", \\\"sep19_decision\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"b_sep18\\\", when=\\\"09/18/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party B\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"3\\\", type=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Revised final-round indication: a price Party B valued at $21.50 per share, comprising $19.00 cash at closing plus options representing 10% of the new equity (strike equal to Party B's initial cost basis; vesting over five years on achievement of the base-case management projections excluding future acquisitions), which Party B valued at $2.50 of incremental value per share. Bidder-valued package — the option component is non-cash and not guaranteed; All cash = No. Formal as a response to the final-indications solicitation (signal 2). Heavy: financing not committed (09/09) and the Committee later noted the third-party debt financing risk.\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Formal\\\", cond=\\\"Heavy\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with a purchase price that Party B valued at $21.50 per share, including $19.00 of cash to be paid at closing and the remaining per share price to be paid in the form of options to be issued to Mac-Gray stockholders, representing 10% of the new equity with a strike price equal to Party B's initial cost basis.” “These options ... would vest on the achievement of the base case management projections (i.e., over five years), excluding any future acquisitions. Party B's proposal stated that it valued the Party B options at $2.50 of incremental value per share.” (p.36) “Party B would likely be financing the transaction with a combination of equity from affiliated funds and third party debt capital, which would involve more risk than the Pamplona-funded CSC/Pamplona proposal” (P-055, p.37).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-053\\\", \\\"P-047\\\", \\\"P-055\\\"], page=36, count=1, review=\\\"Q5; Q6\\\",\\n plow=21.50, phigh=21.50, pkind=\\\"Point\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", currency=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"No\\\", cashclose=19.00,\\n conddetail=NOTCOMM,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-18\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-18\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-18\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"b_sep9\\\", \\\"sep19_decision\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"c_nosub\\\", when=\\\"by 09/18/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party C\\\", what=\\\"Did not submit\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"3\\\", type=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest and did not reiterate its prior $16.00–$17.00 indication in the final-indications solicitation; the filing states it specified no reasons. Stated non-submission; decided by the bidder; no reason given.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest of an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share nor did it specify any reasons in connection therewith.” (p.36) “reported that Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest” (P-054, p.36).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-053\\\", \\\"P-054\\\"], page=36, count=1, review=\\\"Q4\\\",\\n decidedby=\\\"Bidder\\\", exitreason=\\\"Not stated\\\", obasis=\\\"Stated\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-18\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-18\\\", dbasis=\\\"Relative only\\\", dmethod=\\\"Assigned: deadline\\\",\\n related=[\\\"c_sep10\\\", \\\"dl_sep18\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"sep19_decision\\\", when=\\\"09/19/2013\\\", who=\\\"Special Committee\\\", what=\\\"Target decision\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"3\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"After reviewing the three final proposals and the Projections, the Committee considered CSC/Pamplona the most value with greater certainty and less risk (Party B's package was higher on its face but carried option-measurement risk and third-party debt financing), concluded CSC/Pamplona should be able to raise above $20.75, and authorized the Transaction Committee to inform CSC/Pamplona that the Special Committee was prepared to move into exclusivity at $21.25 per share. Mr. MacDonald indicated he would be supportive of $21.25.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “the Special Committee concluded that the revised indication of interest submitted by CSC/Pamplona had the potential of delivering the most value to stockholders, provided greater certainty and involved less potential risk than the other indications. However, the Special Committee also concluded that, primarily in view of potential synergies between Mac-Gray and CSC, CSC/Pamplona should be in a position to increase their offer price above $20.75. The Special Committee then authorized the Transaction Committee to inform CSC/Pamplona that the Special Committee would be prepared to move into exclusivity at a price of $21.25 per share” “at this meeting Mr. MacDonald indicated that he would be supportive of a price of $21.25 per share” (both p.37).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-054\\\", \\\"P-055\\\"], page=37, review=\\\"Q1\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-19\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-19\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-19\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"csc_sep18\\\", \\\"a_reaff\\\", \\\"b_sep18\\\", \\\"r4_open\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"r4_open\\\", when=\\\"09/21/2013\\\", who=\\\"Transaction Committee / CSC/Pamplona\\\",\\n what=\\\"Round opened\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"4\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Round 4 opened: the Transaction Committee proposed moving forward with CSC/Pamplona exclusively for two weeks subject to an increase to $21.25 per share; CSC/Pamplona confirmed the same day that it would increase its all-cash price to $21.25 as a last and best offer provided Mac-Gray agreed to a two-week exclusive negotiation (exclusivity agreement executed 09/24/2013, R044). Round finality: Inferred final — the target moved to definitive negotiation with the selected bidder; no finality announcement to the other bidders. Round-4 bidder: CSC/Pamplona (1 unit).\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “the members of the Transaction Committee called the representative of CSC/Pamplona to propose that Mac-Gray was prepared to move forward with CSC/Pamplona on an exclusive basis for two weeks subject to CSC/Pamplona increasing their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share. Later that same day, the representative of CSC/Pamplona called the members of the Transaction Committee to confirm that CSC/Pamplona were willing to increase their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share as a last and best offer, provided that Mac-Gray agree to a two week period of exclusive negotiations.” (p.37)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-056\\\"], page=37, rfinal=\\\"Inferred final\\\", review=\\\"Q1\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-21\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-21\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-21\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"sep19_decision\\\", \\\"csc_sep21\\\", \\\"excl_granted\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"csc_sep21\\\", when=\\\"09/21/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC/Pamplona\\\", what=\\\"Bid\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"4\\\", type=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"All-cash $21.25 per share last and best offer, conditioned on a two-week exclusive negotiation. Part of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal, which also included no financing contingency, Pamplona's commitment to fund 100% of the capital needed for closing, a $15 million reverse termination fee payable if regulatory clearance is not obtained, and post-signing covenants; exclusivity would automatically terminate if CSC/Pamplona adversely changed the proposal terms. Formal: price confirmed as the parties moved to exclusivity and definitive negotiation (signal 3; the same price was carried into the signed merger agreement).\\\",\\n formality=\\\"Formal\\\", cond=\\\"Light\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “CSC/Pamplona were willing to increase their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share as a last and best offer, provided that Mac-Gray agree to a two week period of exclusive negotiations.” (p.37) “the inclusion of a $15 million \\\"reverse\\\" termination fee payable by CSC/Pamplona to Mac-Gray in the event regulatory clearance is not obtained” “the fact that there would be no financing contingency and that Pamplona was committing to fund 100% of the capital needed for closing, which, together with the all-cash per share purchase price of $21.25, we refer to as the CSC/Pamplona final proposal” (p.37–38).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-056\\\", \\\"P-057\\\", \\\"P-059\\\"], page=37, count=1, review=\\\"Q5\\\",\\n plow=21.25, phigh=21.25, pkind=\\\"Point\\\", porigin=\\\"Stated\\\", currency=\\\"USD\\\", allcash=\\\"Yes\\\", cashclose=21.25,\\n conddetail=COMMITTED.format(excl=\\\"requested (2 wks)\\\"),\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-21\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-21\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-21\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"csc_sep18\\\", \\\"r4_open\\\", \\\"excl_auth\\\", \\\"signed\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"excl_auth\\\", when=\\\"09/23/2013\\\", who=\\\"Special Committee\\\", what=\\\"Exclusivity changed\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"4\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Exclusivity authorized: the Special Committee authorized Mac-Gray to enter into an exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013 on the terms of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal ($21.25 cash; $15 million CSC reverse termination fee if regulatory clearance not obtained; no financing contingency; Pamplona funding 100% of closing capital; automatic termination on adverse change). This followed negotiation of the agreement's terms 09/21–09/23/2013.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “the Special Committee authorized Mac-Gray to enter into an exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013 on the terms included in the CSC/Pamplona final proposal and authorized the Transaction Committee and Goodwin Procter to continue negotiations with CSC/Pamplona” (p.38). Terms: P-057 (p.37–38).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-057\\\", \\\"P-059\\\"], page=38,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-23\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-23\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-23\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"csc_sep21\\\", \\\"excl_granted\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"excl_granted\\\", when=\\\"09/24/2013\\\", who=\\\"CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray\\\", what=\\\"Exclusivity changed\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"4\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Exclusivity granted: CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013, subject to CSC/Pamplona not adversely changing or modifying the CSC/Pamplona final proposal terms. During exclusivity (09/25–10/07/2013) CSC and Pamplona received full access to the electronic data site and to certain management and conducted confirmatory business and legal diligence.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013, subject to certain conditions, including that CSC and Pamplona not adversely change or modify the terms of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal.” “CSC and Pamplona were granted full access to the electronic data site and access to certain members of management and conducted confirmatory business and legal due diligence on Mac-Gray.” (both p.38)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-060\\\", \\\"P-061\\\"], page=38,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-24\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-24\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-24\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"excl_auth\\\", \\\"a_dropped\\\", \\\"b_dropped\\\", \\\"excl_ext\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"a_dropped\\\", when=\\\"by 09/24/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party A\\\", what=\\\"Dropped by target\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"4\\\", type=\\\"Strategic\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Inferred: exclusivity — with exclusivity executed with CSC/Pamplona on 09/24/2013, Party A was displaced from the process; no notice to Party A is reported and no earlier outcome is recorded. Count 1.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Inferred: exclusivity. “On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013” (P-060, p.38); Party A was live with its best-and-final offer when CSC/Pamplona was selected (P-053, p.36; P-055, p.37).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-060\\\", \\\"P-053\\\", \\\"P-055\\\"], page=38, count=1, review=\\\"Q4\\\",\\n decidedby=\\\"Target\\\", exitreason=\\\"Not stated\\\", obasis=\\\"Inferred: exclusivity\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-24\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-24\\\", dbasis=\\\"Relative only\\\", dmethod=\\\"Assigned: decision day\\\",\\n related=[\\\"excl_granted\\\", \\\"a_reaff\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"b_dropped\\\", when=\\\"by 09/24/2013\\\", who=\\\"Party B\\\", what=\\\"Dropped by target\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"4\\\", type=\\\"Financial\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Inferred: exclusivity — with exclusivity executed with CSC/Pamplona on 09/24/2013, Party B was displaced from the process; no notice to Party B is reported and no earlier outcome is recorded. Count 1.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Inferred: exclusivity. “On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013” (P-060, p.38); Party B was live with its $21.50-valued package when CSC/Pamplona was selected (P-053, p.36; P-055, p.37).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-060\\\", \\\"P-053\\\", \\\"P-055\\\"], page=38, count=1, review=\\\"Q4\\\",\\n decidedby=\\\"Target\\\", exitreason=\\\"Not stated\\\", obasis=\\\"Inferred: exclusivity\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"\\\", dto=\\\"2013-09-24\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-24\\\", dbasis=\\\"Relative only\\\", dmethod=\\\"Assigned: decision day\\\",\\n related=[\\\"excl_granted\\\", \\\"b_sep18\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"kirkland\\\", when=\\\"09/25/2013 (earliest observed service; commencement not disclosed)\\\",\\n who=\\\"Kirkland & Ellis LLP — CSC/Pamplona (client)\\\", what=\\\"Adviser service observed\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"4\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona; first observed receiving the initial draft merger agreement from Goodwin Procter on 09/25/2013. Thereafter negotiated the merger agreement, the Pamplona commitment letter (including Pamplona's liability cap) and the voting agreements with Goodwin Procter and counsel for the stockholders through signing. Engagement or selection date not disclosed.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated (service; no engagement date). “On September 25, 2013, Goodwin Procter delivered to Kirkland & Ellis LLP, outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona, whom we refer to as Kirkland, the initial draft of the merger agreement.” (p.38) “Kirkland delivered to Goodwin Procter a revised draft of the Pamplona commitment letter which, among other things, proposed that, in addition to CSC, Pamplona would be responsible in the event CSC failed to consummate the merger, but that Pamplona's liability for damages ... would be limited to an unspecified dollar amount.” (p.39)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-061\\\", \\\"P-064\\\"], page=38,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-25\\\", dto=\\\"\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-09-25\\\", dbasis=\\\"Relative only\\\", dmethod=\\\"Assigned: bound\\\",\\n related=[\\\"excl_granted\\\", \\\"signed\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"moab_resolved\\\", when=\\\"09/23/2013–10/07/2013 (discussions through early October; no rollover determined by 10/07/2013)\\\",\\n who=\\\"Moab (Mr. Rothenberg) / CSC-Pamplona\\\", what=\\\"Material process update\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"4\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Rollover (step 2 — permitted, then resolved without a rollover): Mac-Gray told Mr. Rothenberg on a limited basis of the process status and the CSC/Pamplona negotiations so Moab could resume rollover discussions with CSC/Pamplona; he indicated interest and BofA agreed to arrange and facilitate. Mr. Rothenberg then held discussions with Pamplona; as a result it was determined that Moab would not roll over any shares in the transaction (reported to the Special Committee on 10/07/2013).\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “to provide Moab with the opportunity to resume discussions with CSC/Pamplona regarding a possible equity rollover of Moab's shares in the transaction if Moab still had an interest in such a rollover. Mr. Rothenberg indicated he would like to discuss the possibility of an equity rollover with CSC/Pamplona” (p.38). “Mr. Rothenberg engaged in various discussions with representatives of Pamplona during this time to discuss a possible rollover of Moab shares. As a result of such discussions, it was determined that Moab would not rollover any Moab shares in the transaction.” (p.38) “Mr. Daoust reported to the Special Committee that, after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona, it was determined that Moab would not rollover any Moab shares in the transaction.” (p.39)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-058\\\", \\\"P-061\\\", \\\"P-065\\\"], page=39,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-09-23\\\", dto=\\\"2013-10-07\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-10-07\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported interval\\\", dmethod=\\\"Assigned: decision day\\\",\\n related=[\\\"moab_denied\\\", \\\"moab_proxy\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"excl_ext\\\", when=\\\"10/12/2013 (letter agreement; extension sought 10/09–10/11)\\\",\\n who=\\\"CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray\\\", what=\\\"Exclusivity changed\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"4\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Exclusivity extended: with exclusivity due to expire at 5 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013 and open issues remaining, CSC/Pamplona requested an extension; the Special Committee objected to the $15 million Mac-Gray termination fee and would not extend unless a lower amount was agreed; CSC/Pamplona agreed to the $11 million fee, and the parties executed a letter agreement extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on 10/15/2013. Scheduled (not observed) end: the merger agreement was signed 10/14/2013.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “On October 12, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed a letter agreement extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on October 15, 2013.” (p.41) “the Special Committee continued to object to the $15 million Mac-Gray termination fee proposed by CSC/Pamplona and would not be willing to extend exclusivity unless a lower amount were agreed to” “authorized to extend the exclusivity agreement until 11:59 p.m. on ET on October 15, 2013 if CSC/Pamplona would agree to a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million” (p.40) — “Shortly following that conversation, the representative of CSC/Pamplona telephoned Mr. Daoust and agreed to the $11 million Mac-Gray termination fee.” (p.40–41)\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-069\\\", \\\"P-071\\\", \\\"P-072\\\"], page=41,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-10-12\\\", dto=\\\"2013-10-12\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-10-12\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"excl_granted\\\", \\\"signed\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"signed\\\", when=\\\"10/14/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray / Special Committee / Board of Directors / CSC-Pamplona\\\",\\n what=\\\"Merger agreement signed\\\", process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"4\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Agreed consideration: $21.25 per share in cash, without interest and less applicable withholding (whole-company merger; Mac-Gray survives as a wholly-owned subsidiary of Parent). The Special Committee unanimously recommended and the Board unanimously approved and adopted the merger agreement; BofA Merrill Lynch delivered its oral fairness opinion, confirmed in writing dated 10/14/2013. The merger agreement was executed later that day; the Pamplona commitment letter was delivered ($594 million committed by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P.; no financing condition; Pamplona and the Buyer Entities jointly and severally liable for damages, with Pamplona's liability capped at $50 million and the Buyer Entities' liability unlimited); Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement and the MacDonald voting agreements (entered 09/27/2013) became effective — approximately 15% of shares subject to voting agreements. Mac-Gray termination fee $11 million; CSC reverse termination fee $15 million. Signing is not an extra submitted bid: numeric bid-price cells and formality/conditionality cells are blank on this row.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “the Special Committee unanimously determined to recommend to the Board that the merger agreement and the merger were advisable and in the best interests of Mac-Gray's stockholders” (p.41). “the merger agreement was executed, the Pamplona commitment letter was delivered, Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement and the Mac-Donald voting agreements became effective.” (p.41) “Parent will fund the merger consideration from an aggregate of $594 million of capital, ... committed pursuant to a commitment letter delivered to the Buyer Entities by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. dated as of October 14, 2013” (p.6; also Annex A Section 5.08, p. A-30). “Mac-Gray has agreed to pay Parent $11 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances ... Parent has agreed to pay Mac-Gray $15 million ...” (p.10; also p.80–81).\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-075\\\", \\\"P-076\\\", \\\"P-077\\\", \\\"X-002\\\", \\\"X-005\\\", \\\"X-026\\\", \\\"X-017\\\", \\\"X-018\\\", \\\"X-006\\\"], page=41, review=\\\"Q5\\\",\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-10-14\\\", dto=\\\"2013-10-14\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-10-14\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"csc_sep21\\\", \\\"excl_ext\\\", \\\"announced\\\", \\\"bofa_new\\\"]),\\n\\ndict(key=\\\"announced\\\", when=\\\"10/15/2013\\\", who=\\\"Mac-Gray and CSC\\\", what=\\\"Merger announced\\\",\\n process=\\\"1\\\", round=\\\"4\\\", type=\\\"\\\",\\n terms=\\\"Joint public announcement of the execution of the merger agreement, made before the U.S. stock markets opened. Public disclosure of the transaction; no earlier public sale-process announcement or leak is reported. No go-shop is provided; no post-signing competing proposal is disclosed in the proxy statement.\\\",\\n evidence=\\\"Stated. “On October 15, 2013, before the U.S. stock markets opened, Mac-Gray and CSC jointly announced the execution of the merger agreement.” (p.41). Absence of a go-shop: the merger agreement prohibits solicitation subject to a fiduciary out — “if, prior to the adoption of the merger agreement by Mac-Gray stockholders, Mac-Gray receives an unsolicited bona fide acquisition proposal in writing ... Mac-Gray may ... enter into, maintain and participate in discussions or negotiations” (p.8); no go-shop provision is described.\\\",\\n source=[\\\"P-078\\\", \\\"X-004\\\"], page=41,\\n dfrom=\\\"2013-10-15\\\", dto=\\\"2013-10-15\\\", wdate=\\\"2013-10-15\\\", dbasis=\\\"Reported day\\\", dmethod=\\\"Reported\\\",\\n related=[\\\"signed\\\"]),\\n]\\n\\n# Order of keys defines reading order; sanity check that it matches list order\\nKEYS = [r['key'] for r in ROWS]\\nassert len(KEYS) == len(set(KEYS)), \\\"duplicate keys\\\"\\n\", \"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/ledger_data.py\"}"},"time":{"start":1789824762530,"end":1789824823249}}}}
