{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824854532,"sessionID":"ses_f462a5515ffeVXejhZ4OL349Hs","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9dfda4d001QQPHXpCTaF8Q7x","sessionID":"ses_f462a5515ffeVXejhZ4OL349Hs","messageID":"msg_0b9dfaf77001c710kTFqH4hdlM","type":"tool","id":"call_00_tENPPNzLlHrqRYUvKyye0052","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport io\ns = open('ledger_data.py', encoding='utf-8').read()\n\nfixes = [\n# goodwin evidence - remove spliced quote\n(\"“at an in-person meeting of the Board on April 5, 2013, ... representatives from BofA Merrill Lynch and Goodwin Procter LLP, outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray, were also in attendance” — first narrative mention in the background is the May 9, 2013 meeting (p.27–28).\",\n \"“representatives from BofA Merrill Lynch and Goodwin Procter LLP, outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray, were also in attendance for all or portions of the meeting” (p.27) — first narrative mention of Goodwin Procter in the background (May 9, 2013 Board meeting).\"),\n# contact_strat / contact_fin fixed quotes\n(\"“a total of 50 parties, ... 15 of which were potential strategic buyers and 35 of which were potential financial buyers”\",\n \"“a total of 50 parties, including CSC and Pamplona, who together we refer to as CSC/Pamplona, and Party A, to solicit potential interest in a transaction with Mac-Gray, 15 of which were potential strategic buyers and 35 of which were potential financial buyers, including private equity firms”\"),\n# dlset_sep9 authorization quote\n(\"“the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to send a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona once all four of the bidders' due diligence was substantially complete requesting that ... such party submit a revised written proposal in order to continue in the process”\",\n \"“the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to send a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona once all four of the bidders' due diligence was substantially complete requesting that, in light of the results of the respective party's due diligence, such party submit a revised written proposal in order to continue in the process”\"),\n# macd_decline quote\n(\"“provided Mr. MacDonald with a limited overview of the status of the Special Committee's review of strategic alternatives ... so that Mr. MacDonald could consider whether he continued to have an interest in potentially rolling over any of his Mac-Gray shares in a transaction. During this call,\",\n \"“provided Mr. MacDonald with a limited overview of the status of the Special Committee's review of strategic alternatives, including the decision to engage in strategic alternatives process, and the negotiations between Mac-Gray and CSC/Pamplona so that Mr. MacDonald could consider whether he continued to have an interest in potentially rolling over any of his Mac-Gray shares in a transaction. During this call,\"),\n# b_sep18 options quote\n(\"“These options ... would vest on the achievement of the base case management projections (i.e., over five years), excluding any future acquisitions. Party B's proposal stated that it valued the Party B options at $2.50 of incremental value per share.”\",\n \"“These options, which we refer to as the Party B options, would vest on the achievement of the base case management projections (i.e., over five years), excluding any future acquisitions. Party B's proposal stated that it valued the Party B options at $2.50 of incremental value per share.”\"),\n# kirkland quote\n(\"“Kirkland delivered to Goodwin Procter a revised draft of the Pamplona commitment letter which, among other things, proposed that, in addition to CSC, Pamplona would be responsible in the event CSC failed to consummate the merger, but that Pamplona's liability for damages ... would be limited to an unspecified dollar amount.”\",\n \"“Kirkland delivered to Goodwin Procter a revised draft of the Pamplona commitment letter which, among other things, proposed that, in addition to CSC, Pamplona would be responsible in the event CSC failed to consummate the merger, but that Pamplona's liability for damages resulting from a breach of the merger agreement would be limited to an unspecified dollar amount.”\"),\n# signed financing quote\n(\"“Parent will fund the merger consideration from an aggregate of $594 million of capital, ... committed pursuant to a commitment letter delivered to the Buyer Entities by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. dated as of October 14, 2013”\",\n \"“Parent will fund the merger consideration from an aggregate of $594 million of capital, which we refer to as the Pamplona commitment amount and which is committed pursuant to a commitment letter delivered to the Buyer Entities by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. dated as of October 14, 2013, which we refer to as the Pamplona commitment letter.”\"),\n# signed fees quote\n(\"“Mac-Gray has agreed to pay Parent $11 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances ... Parent has agreed to pay Mac-Gray $15 million ...”\",\n \"“Mac-Gray has agreed to pay Parent $11 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances, which we refer to as the Mac-Gray termination fee. Parent has agreed to pay Mac-Gray $15 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances, which we refer to as the Parent termination fee.”\"),\n# announced quote\n(\"“if, prior to the adoption of the merger agreement by Mac-Gray stockholders, Mac-Gray receives an unsolicited bona fide acquisition proposal in writing ... Mac-Gray may ... enter into, maintain and participate in discussions or negotiations”\",\n \"“prior to the adoption of the merger agreement by Mac-Gray stockholders, if Mac-Gray receives an unsolicited bona fide acquisition proposal in writing from a third party after the date of the merger agreement” “then Mac-Gray may furnish to such third party non-public information relating to Mac-Gray pursuant to a confidentiality agreement meeting certain requirements as set forth in the merger agreement and afford such third party access to the businesses, properties, assets and personnel of Mac-Gray or any of its subsidiaries and enter into, maintain and participate in discussions or negotiations with such third party or otherwise cooperate with or assist or participate in, or facilitate, any such discussions or negotiations”\"),\n]\nfor old, new in fixes:\n    if old not in s:\n        print(\"NOT FOUND:\", old[:90])\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\nopen('ledger_data.py','w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint(\"done\")\nEOF\npython3 validate_quotes.py"},"output":"done\ntotal failures: 0\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"done\ntotal failures: 0\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport io\\ns = open('ledger_data.py', encoding='utf-8').read()\\n\\nfixes = [\\n# goodwin evidence - remove spliced quote\\n(\\\"“at an in-person meeting of the Board on April 5, 2013, ... representatives from BofA Merrill Lynch and Goodwin Procter LLP, outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray, were also in attendance” — first narrative mention in the background is the May 9, 2013 meeting (p.27–28).\\\",\\n \\\"“representatives from BofA Merrill Lynch and Goodwin Procter LLP, outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray, were also in attendance for all or portions of the meeting” (p.27) — first narrative mention of Goodwin Procter in the background (May 9, 2013 Board meeting).\\\"),\\n# contact_strat / contact_fin fixed quotes\\n(\\\"“a total of 50 parties, ... 15 of which were potential strategic buyers and 35 of which were potential financial buyers”\\\",\\n \\\"“a total of 50 parties, including CSC and Pamplona, who together we refer to as CSC/Pamplona, and Party A, to solicit potential interest in a transaction with Mac-Gray, 15 of which were potential strategic buyers and 35 of which were potential financial buyers, including private equity firms”\\\"),\\n# dlset_sep9 authorization quote\\n(\\\"“the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to send a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona once all four of the bidders' due diligence was substantially complete requesting that ... such party submit a revised written proposal in order to continue in the process”\\\",\\n \\\"“the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to send a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona once all four of the bidders' due diligence was substantially complete requesting that, in light of the results of the respective party's due diligence, such party submit a revised written proposal in order to continue in the process”\\\"),\\n# macd_decline quote\\n(\\\"“provided Mr. MacDonald with a limited overview of the status of the Special Committee's review of strategic alternatives ... so that Mr. MacDonald could consider whether he continued to have an interest in potentially rolling over any of his Mac-Gray shares in a transaction. During this call,\\\",\\n \\\"“provided Mr. MacDonald with a limited overview of the status of the Special Committee's review of strategic alternatives, including the decision to engage in strategic alternatives process, and the negotiations between Mac-Gray and CSC/Pamplona so that Mr. MacDonald could consider whether he continued to have an interest in potentially rolling over any of his Mac-Gray shares in a transaction. During this call,\\\"),\\n# b_sep18 options quote\\n(\\\"“These options ... would vest on the achievement of the base case management projections (i.e., over five years), excluding any future acquisitions. Party B's proposal stated that it valued the Party B options at $2.50 of incremental value per share.”\\\",\\n \\\"“These options, which we refer to as the Party B options, would vest on the achievement of the base case management projections (i.e., over five years), excluding any future acquisitions. Party B's proposal stated that it valued the Party B options at $2.50 of incremental value per share.”\\\"),\\n# kirkland quote\\n(\\\"“Kirkland delivered to Goodwin Procter a revised draft of the Pamplona commitment letter which, among other things, proposed that, in addition to CSC, Pamplona would be responsible in the event CSC failed to consummate the merger, but that Pamplona's liability for damages ... would be limited to an unspecified dollar amount.”\\\",\\n \\\"“Kirkland delivered to Goodwin Procter a revised draft of the Pamplona commitment letter which, among other things, proposed that, in addition to CSC, Pamplona would be responsible in the event CSC failed to consummate the merger, but that Pamplona's liability for damages resulting from a breach of the merger agreement would be limited to an unspecified dollar amount.”\\\"),\\n# signed financing quote\\n(\\\"“Parent will fund the merger consideration from an aggregate of $594 million of capital, ... committed pursuant to a commitment letter delivered to the Buyer Entities by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. dated as of October 14, 2013”\\\",\\n \\\"“Parent will fund the merger consideration from an aggregate of $594 million of capital, which we refer to as the Pamplona commitment amount and which is committed pursuant to a commitment letter delivered to the Buyer Entities by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. dated as of October 14, 2013, which we refer to as the Pamplona commitment letter.”\\\"),\\n# signed fees quote\\n(\\\"“Mac-Gray has agreed to pay Parent $11 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances ... Parent has agreed to pay Mac-Gray $15 million ...”\\\",\\n \\\"“Mac-Gray has agreed to pay Parent $11 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances, which we refer to as the Mac-Gray termination fee. Parent has agreed to pay Mac-Gray $15 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances, which we refer to as the Parent termination fee.”\\\"),\\n# announced quote\\n(\\\"“if, prior to the adoption of the merger agreement by Mac-Gray stockholders, Mac-Gray receives an unsolicited bona fide acquisition proposal in writing ... Mac-Gray may ... enter into, maintain and participate in discussions or negotiations”\\\",\\n \\\"“prior to the adoption of the merger agreement by Mac-Gray stockholders, if Mac-Gray receives an unsolicited bona fide acquisition proposal in writing from a third party after the date of the merger agreement” “then Mac-Gray may furnish to such third party non-public information relating to Mac-Gray pursuant to a confidentiality agreement meeting certain requirements as set forth in the merger agreement and afford such third party access to the businesses, properties, assets and personnel of Mac-Gray or any of its subsidiaries and enter into, maintain and participate in discussions or negotiations with such third party or otherwise cooperate with or assist or participate in, or facilitate, any such discussions or negotiations”\\\"),\\n]\\nfor old, new in fixes:\\n    if old not in s:\\n        print(\\\"NOT FOUND:\\\", old[:90])\\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\\nopen('ledger_data.py','w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\\nprint(\\\"done\\\")\\nEOF\\npython3 validate_quotes.py\"}"},"time":{"start":1789824850509,"end":1789824854532}}}}
