owed 09/19). The exclusivity expiry (10/12 5 p.m. ET; extended 10/12 to 10/15 11:59 p.m. ET) is recorded as Exclusivity c\n   WHY: Consideration evidence: “reviewed the preliminary indications of interest received from Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona as well as the Party A June 21 proposal” (p.33); “held a telephonic meeting to review the revised \n--- [4] Q3 | NDA population, the 16-signer residual cohort and its assigned date\n   REC: Keep the 20-signer population as 4 individually dated signers plus a 16-signer residual financial cohort (18 financial − Party B − Party C), Count 16, with terms on a Mac-Gray form individually negotiated without material variance. The residual row carries the reported two-month signing window (working date 06/24/2013, Assigned: bound — the first day of that series) as a display convention so the \n   WHY: Filing: “a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C), entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray on a fo\n--- [5] Q4 | Inferred closings and outcome agency\n   REC: Keep the three inferred closing rows: (1) R021 — 16 residual financial signers, Did not submit, Count 16, Inferred: residual, at the 07/23/2013 deadline; (2) R046 — Party A, Dropped by target, Count 1, Inferred: exclusivity, 09/24/2013; (3) R047 — Party B, same. Keep R040 (Party C, Did not submit, stated) as a stated outcome with agency Bidder and reason Not stated, and do not close Party C again \n   WHY: Inference basis: the four bidders are the only continuing participants after 07/25 (“each of the four interested bidders”, p.33–34); exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona executed 09/24 (p.38). Party C: “Party C did not submit a\n--- [6] Q5 | Formality and conditions classifications\n   REC: Keep: the three later CSC/Pamplona bids Light (committed financing; no diligence condition reported; exclusivity requests do not change the level); all other party bids He