e Mr. MacDonald and Mr. Rothenberg from the Board's evaluation of strategic alternatives and any negotiations with third parties that might take place” (p.30). “a total of 50 parties, including CSC and Pamplona, who together we refer to as CSC/Pamplona, and Party A, to solicit potential interest in a transaction with Mac-Gray, 15 of which were potential strategic buyers and 35 of which were potential financial buyers, including private equity firm\nSource: P-019; P-021; P-022; P-023\nReview: Q1\nRow id: R011\nInclude: Yes\nDate from: 2013-06-24 00:00:00\nDate to: 2013-06-24 00:00:00\nWorking date: 2013-06-24 00:00:00\nDate basis: Reported day\nDate method: Reported\nDue date: 2013-07-23 00:00:00\nRound finality: Not final\nPage: 31\nRelated rows: R010; R003; R012; R019\nDeal: Mac-Gray\n\n====================================================================================================\n#: 21\nWhen: by 07/23/2013\nWho: 16 residual financial NDA signers\nWhat happened: Did not submit\nProcess: 1\nRound: 1\nType: Financial\nTerms or outcome: Inferred: residual — 20 NDA signers (2 strategic + 18 financial) − 4 individually recorded participants (Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona) = 16 residual financial signers with no preliminary indication of interest submitted by the 07/23/2013 deadline; the filing names no other submitters, and the 07/25/2013 Special Committee review addressed only Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona and the standing Party A proposal. Base assumes the residual signers had signed by and were eligible for the solicitation; the filing dates their signatures only as a two-month window. No motive, identity or voluntary withdrawal inferred.\nWhy and evidence: Inferred: residual. “a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C), entered into confidentiality agreements” (P-023, p.32); “representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch reviewed the preliminary indicat