{"type":"text","timestamp":1789825149355,"sessionID":"ses_f462a5515ffeVXejhZ4OL349Hs","part":{"id":"prt_0b9e4545d0015sMgX4x0zIfXn8","sessionID":"ses_f462a5515ffeVXejhZ4OL349Hs","messageID":"msg_0b9e446f4001wUaNKOA9aLra3x","type":"text","text":"The workbook is complete and verified. Here's the delivery.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n**`extraction/mac-gray.xlsx`** — four visible sheets (Deal ledger, Summary, Questions, Source text) plus hidden AI original and Lists. The ledger holds **52 rows** built from the DEFM14A alone; the Source text sheet holds the complete Background of the Merger (78 paragraphs, P-001–P-078) plus every additional passage used (28, X-001–X-028), with page numbers.\n\n## What happened (plain account)\n\nMac-Gray reviewed strategic options with BofA Merrill Lynch from April 2013; after Moab's proxy contest changed the board, a six-director Special Committee launched a sale process on June 24, 2013, approaching 50 parties (15 strategic, 35 financial). Twenty signed confidentiality agreements; four advanced — strategic Party A and CSC/Pamplona (CSC ServiceWorks, a Pamplona Capital portfolio company) plus financial bidders Party B and Party C. July indications of $15.00–$19.00 led to staged disclosure (financial bidders got broad data-site access; strategics got limited access, customer data withheld). September revised proposals ran $16.00–$19.50, with Party B proposing $19.00 cash plus options it valued at $2.50. In the final round (due September 18), CSC/Pamplona bid $20.75 all cash with committed financing, Party A reiterated $18–$19 as best and final, Party B offered its cash-plus-options package, and Party C did not submit. The Committee chose CSC/Pamplona and negotiated **$21.25 all cash** in exchange for two-week exclusivity (September 24, extended to October 15); the merger agreement was signed **October 14** and announced **October 15, 2013**. No go-shop and no post-signing competing proposal is disclosed; closing was expected in 2014 and is not observed in the filing.\n\n## Round map used (see Q1)\n\n- **Round 0:** April 5 exploration authorization, April 8 Party A contact, June 21 Party A proposal ($17–19).\n- **R1** (opened 6/24; anchor = launch decision; first outreach within days): 20 NDAs, indications due 7/23 — *Late bids accepted* (B 7/24, C 7/24–25 considered). 4 advancing.\n- **R2** (7/25): staged disclosure, management presentations; revised proposals due 9/9 — *Late bids accepted* (A, C on 9/10). 4 bidders.\n- **R3** (9/11): first request for final indications, due 9/18 — *Enforced*; 3 submissions + C non-submission. *Announced as final*.\n- **R4** (9/21): exclusivity/definitive negotiation with CSC/Pamplona → signing. *Inferred final*.\n\n## Most consequential review items (recommendations in Questions)\n\n1. **Q1** — R1 anchor (6/24 decision vs the 4/8 contact and 6/21 proposal, both kept as round-0 rows); R4 boundary (9/21 vs 9/19 authorization or 9/24 execution); single process (the 2011-2012 Discussions were a Mac-Gray buy-side mandate).\n2. **Q3/Q4** — the 16-signer residual cohort and its inferred “Did not submit” at 7/23; its base assumes all residual signers were eligible for that solicitation (their signing dates are only a two-month window). Party A and Party B closings at exclusivity are inferred; Party C's non-submission is stated and not re-closed.\n3. **Q5** — formality/conditions: the September 18 responses are Formal (final-solicitation responses); all earlier indications Informal; “Heavy by context” applies to pre-access indications; no late-reconfirmation row was created (the §9.1 test fails for CSC/Pamplona's Formal, Inferred-final position).\n4. **Q6** — Party B's $21.50 is a bidder-valued package ($19 cash + options), All cash = No, $19.00 in Cash at closing.\n5. **Q2/Q7** — deadline treatments and the exclusivity extension; working-date conventions (cohort bound date; “by” inferred rows); the source typo “July 27, 2103” retained with proposed correction.\n\n## Checks (Section 13) and limitations\n\n- **Passed programmatically:** sort order (Working date + #), date-basis/method pairings and bounds, every quotation recoverable from its cited paragraphs, hyperlink targets, drop-down values vs controlled lists, 20-NDA and 50-contact reconciliations, per-stage balance (20−16=4 → 4 → 4−1=3 → 3−2=1), AI original matching the delivered baseline, unique Row ids.\n- **Qualified:** all eight checks carry preserved source limitations (undated residual signer window; layout duplication and typo retained; inferred rows state only exit-by-transition).\n- **Not run / unsupported:** no spreadsheet application was available to test — LibreOffice crashes on any file in this environment, and the file was not opened in Excel. So the Summary formulas were computed programmatically (not recalculated by an application), and the conditional-formatting change highlighting (red bold vs AI original by Row id) is built but unverified in Excel. No other unsupported features: links, validations, filters, groups and collapsed columns are created and checked structurally.","time":{"start":1789825143901,"end":1789825149355}}}
